    modelNote: "The total is your guest count multiplied by the per-guest all-in range for your event type and city tier, and each category is its published weight of that total. The wedding ranges come from the published Indian event guides checked 12 November 2026: a 200-guest Tier 2 wedding costs ₹8–15 lakh and a metro one ₹15–30 lakh (sabtools), a 300-guest Tier 1 wedding costs about ₹15 lakh (plantoday), and a mid-range wedding runs ₹3,000–₹8,000 a guest (plan4event). Corporate events run ₹1,000–₹3,000 a head a day and premium conferences ₹5,000–₹10,000 (plan4event); a metro one-day conference runs ₹5,000–₹12,000 a head (venueexchange). The engagement range is 60% of the wedding range in the same tier and the Tier 3 wedding range is scaled from the Tier 2 range by the published catering tier ratio — both are labelled planning assumptions, not quoted rates. Totals exclude GST: vendor quotes usually exclude 18% GST, so add it before you present a corporate budget.",
    steps: [
      ["Pick your event type", "Wedding, corporate event, birthday party, engagement or conference. The same 200 guests cost very different amounts at a wedding and at a team offsite — the event type decides the per-guest range."],
      ["Enter your guest count", "From 10 to 2,000 guests. Fix this first: every other number depends on headcount, and a last-minute jump of 50 guests moves the total by lakhs."],
      ["Pick your city tier", "Metro, Tier 1, Tier 2 or Tier 3. Catering alone runs ₹1,200–₹1,800 a plate in a Tier 1 city and ₹500–₹800 in a Tier 3 town — the tier moves every line of the budget."],
      ["Read the range, then get quotes", "The tool gives a total range, a per-guest range and a category split. Take the range to vendors, ask for the per-head price including service staff and crockery, and get the 18% GST in writing."]
    ],
