    overview: "It projects what a single, one-time investment could grow to at a steady yearly return. The whole amount starts compounding from day one, so time does most of the work: at 12% a year, ₹1 lakh becomes ₹3,10,585 in 10 years and ₹9,64,629 in 20 years — doubling the period more than triples the value. The calculator also shows what the final value buys in today's money, after inflation, and what the same total would reach if you put it in month by month as a SIP instead — because a lump sum only wins on paper if the return stays steady, and real markets do not move in a straight line.",
