        title: "₹12,00,000 CTC, basic 50%, PF on the ceiling",
        body: "A ₹12,00,000 CTC with basic at 50% (₹6,00,000) and PF on the ₹25,000 wage ceiling. The employer PF is ₹36,000 and the gratuity provision is ₹28,846, so the gross salary is ₹11,35,154. Your own PF is ₹36,000 and professional tax is ₹2,400; the taxable income is ₹10,60,154, so the slab tax of ₹46,015 is cancelled by the section 87A rebate and the income tax is ₹0. You take home ₹10,96,754 a year — ₹91,396 a month, 91.4% of the CTC. This is zimyo.com's worked example: it publishes ₹91,395 a month — ₹1 less — because it uses the rounded 4.81% for gratuity (₹28,860) instead of the exact 15/26 (₹28,846)."
