        body: "The same ₹12,00,000 CTC, but with PF on the full basic of ₹50,000 a month instead of the ₹25,000 ceiling. The employer PF doubles to ₹72,000, so the gross salary falls to ₹10,99,154, and your own PF is ₹72,000 too. The income tax is still ₹0 — the taxable income of ₹10,24,154 is under the ₹12 lakh rebate limit — but you take home ₹10,24,754 a year, ₹85,396 a month: ₹6,000 a month less than on the ceiling, from one toggle. This is paychequecalc.com's example, reproduced exactly."
