        body: "A ₹12,00,000 CTC with basic at 40% (₹4,80,000) and PF on the ₹25,000 ceiling. The employer PF is ₹36,000 and the gratuity provision is ₹23,077, so the gross salary is ₹11,40,923 — higher than at 50% basic, because less of the CTC is tied up in PF and gratuity. Your own PF is ₹36,000 and professional tax is ₹2,400; the income tax is ₹0. You take home ₹11,02,523 a year — ₹91,877 a month, 91.9% of the CTC. This is layoffnext.com's worked example, reproduced exactly."
