    overview: "It turns five inputs — your sex, age, weight, height and activity level — into the calories your body burns at rest and the calories you burn in a whole day. On the sample, Priya's BMR is 1,370 kcal a day and her TDEE at lightly active is 1,884 kcal a day. The same body burns very different amounts at different activity levels: at sedentary her TDEE would be 1,644 kcal a day, and at extra active it would be 2,603. That is why the activity level matters as much as the BMR itself — picking the wrong level moves the daily target by 300–500 kcal. The calculator also gives the daily targets for losing weight (500 kcal below TDEE, never below the BMR), maintaining weight (the TDEE itself) and gaining weight (300 kcal above TDEE), plus the BMI for the same figures.",
