    "overviewTitle": "What does a discount calculator do?",
    "overview": "It takes the original price and the discount and works out what you actually pay. On the sample — ₹1,999 at 25% off — the discount is ₹499.75 and the sale price is ₹1,499.25. The calculator also shows the effective discount (25% here), and, with GST switched on, the tax on the discounted price and the total payable. Two discounts in a row are applied one after the other, never added: 20% then 10% on ₹10,000 gives ₹7,200, which is 28% off, not 30%.",
