    "overviewTitle": "What does a capital gains tax calculator do?",
    "overview": "It works out the tax on the profit from selling an asset — the sale value minus the buy value — at the rate that applies to that asset and that holding period. On the sample — three sales with a ₹9,00,000 gain between them — the tax is ₹1,08,550: ₹20,800 on an equity gain sold in 6 months, ₹22,750 on an equity gain sold in 18 months, and ₹65,000 on a ₹5,00,000 gain on another asset sold in 36 months, each including 4% cess. The Income Tax Calculator works out tax on salary and other income under the slabs, and it states that capital gains are not covered there; this tool covers only capital gains, at the special rates. Everything is worked out in your browser; nothing is sent anywhere.",
