        "Who has to pay advance tax?",
        "Anyone whose estimated tax for the year, after subtracting TDS and TCS, is ₹10,000 or more. That mainly means freelancers, consultants, business owners, landlords and investors, whose income has little or no tax deducted — and salaried people with sizeable interest, dividend or capital-gains income on top of the salary. Resident senior citizens aged 60 or over with no business or professional income are exempt and pay everything as self-assessment tax at filing time."
