    "mistakesTitle": "Five mistakes that add interest you did not need to pay",
    "modelNote": "Net advance tax = estimated tax − TDS / TCS. It is due only when the net liability is ₹10,000 or more. The instalments are cumulative: 15% by 15 June, 45% by 15 September, 75% by 15 December, 100% by 15 March — presumptive taxpayers pay 100% by 15 March. Section 425 interest = 3% of each shortfall on the first three dates and 1% on the last, each shortfall rounded down to ₹100, with no interest on June if 12% was paid or on September if 36% was paid. Section 424 interest = 1% a month from 1 April on the unpaid balance when under 90% was paid by 31 March. Money is rounded to paise.",
    "notice": "This is a calculation for planning only, not tax advice. The interest is worked out on the tax you enter, rounded down to the nearest ₹100 per instalment, and assumes the whole balance is paid in the month you choose. Section 423 interest for filing the return late is not included. A shortfall caused by capital gains, dividends or newly started business income you could not foresee carries no section 425 interest if the tax is paid in the remaining instalments or by 31 March — this tool does not apply that relief. Resident senior citizens aged 60 or over with no business or professional income are exempt from advance tax entirely.",
    "overview": "Advance tax is income tax paid in instalments during the year the income is earned, not in one sum at filing. On the sample — ₹1,50,000 of tax for FY 2026-27 with no TDS — ₹22,500 is due by 15 June, ₹45,000 more by 15 September, ₹45,000 more by 15 December and ₹37,500 by 15 March. Paying ₹15,000 / ₹50,000 / ₹90,000 / ₹1,20,000 instead leaves shortfalls of ₹7,500 / ₹17,500 / ₹22,500 / ₹30,000, and the interest is ₹1,725 under section 425 plus ₹1,200 under section 424 — ₹2,925 in all, on a total payable of ₹1,52,925. The Income Tax calculator works out the year's tax; the TDS calculator works out what is deducted; this tool works out when to pay it and what late payment costs. Everything is worked out in your browser; nothing is sent anywhere.",
