    "mistakesTitle": "Common brokerage mistakes to avoid",
    "modelNote": "Turnover = buy value + sell value (for options, the premium values). Brokerage is charged per executed order: Zerodha ₹0 on delivery, the lower of ₹20 or 0.03% on intraday and futures, ₹20 flat on options; Groww and Angel One the lower of ₹20 or 0.1% (minimum ₹5) on equity and ₹20 flat on F&O; Upstox ₹20 flat on delivery, the lower of ₹20 or 0.1% on intraday, the lower of ₹20 or 0.05% on futures and ₹20 on options; flat ₹20 is ₹20 per order everywhere. STT: delivery 0.1% on buy and sell, intraday 0.025% on sell, futures 0.05% on sell, options 0.15% of the premium sold. Exchange transaction charges: NSE equity 0.00307%, futures 0.00183%, options 0.03553% of premium; BSE equity 0.00375%, futures 0, options 0.0325% of premium. SEBI fee ₹10 per crore of turnover. Stamp duty on the buy side: delivery 0.015%, intraday 0.003%, futures 0.002%, options 0.003%. DP charge on delivery sells only: Zerodha ₹15.34 per scrip including GST, other brokers ₹20 + GST (₹23.60). GST 18% on brokerage + exchange charges + SEBI fee. Break-even is the sell price at which net profit is exactly zero. Money is rounded to paise.",
    "notice": "This is an estimate for planning only, not investment advice. Rates are as of November 2026: NSE transaction charges from 1 March 2026 and STT from 1 April 2026 (Finance Act 2026). Confirm the figures on your contract note, which is the final record. Call-and-trade and auto-square-off fees, account maintenance charges, pledge fees, payment-gateway fees and interest on margin funding are not included. STT rates assume STT-paid trades on a recognised exchange. Options STT and exchange charges are on the premium, not the contract value.",
    "overview": "A brokerage calculator adds up every charge on a trade, not just the broker's fee. On the sample — 100 shares bought at ₹1,000 and sold the same day at ₹1,010 through Zerodha — the gross profit is ₹1,000, but the charges are ₹82.97: ₹40.00 brokerage, ₹25.25 STT, ₹6.17 exchange charges, ₹0.20 SEBI fee, ₹3.00 stamp duty and ₹8.35 GST. The net profit is ₹917.03, and the price must reach ₹1,000.83 before the trade makes anything at all. The Share Average calculator works out your average buy price; the Capital Gains Tax calculator works out the tax on the profit at filing time; this tool works out what the trade itself costs. Everything is worked out in your browser; nothing is sent anywhere.",
    "overviewTitle": "What does a brokerage calculator do?",
