    "inputNote": "Start with the average of your last 12 electricity bills — monthly units, not the bill amount — and the tariff from the energy-charge line of the bill. Then pick the system size, or take the suggested size the calculator works out for your units. Add your shadow-free roof area if you know it, tick the special-category box only if your state or UT is one, and replace the cost per kW with your vendor's written quote. The sample — 300 units a month, 2.5 kW, ₹7 a unit, ₹3 surplus, 40 m² of roof, ₹60,000 a kW — is filled in.",
