    "mistakesTitle": "Common DA mistakes to avoid",
    "modelNote": "DA = basic pay × DA rate %, rounded to the nearest rupee (fractions of 50 paise and above round up to the next rupee, smaller fractions are ignored). DR for pensioners is the same percentage of basic pension, rounded up to the next rupee. DA a year = DA a month × 12. Pay with DA = basic pay + DA. Arrears a month = DA at the new rate − DA at the old rate, each rounded first; total arrears = arrears a month × months paid at the old rate. NPS deduction = 10% of the arrears, for employees under NPS only, rounded to the nearest rupee; arrears in hand = total arrears − NPS deduction. DA as a share of pay with DA = DA ÷ pay with DA × 100. The current rate is 63% from 1 July 2026 (Cabinet approval 28 October 2026; DoE OM No. 1/2(i)/2026-E.II(B) dated 29 October 2026); 60% ran from 1 January 2026.",
    "notice": "This is an estimate for planning only, not pay advice. Rules as of November 2026: DA is 63% of basic pay from 1 July 2026 (Union Cabinet approval, 28 October 2026; Department of Expenditure OM No. 1/2(i)/2026-E.II(B) dated 29 October 2026), up from 60% from 1 January 2026. Pensioners get Dearness Relief at the same rate on basic pension. DA is paid on basic pay only — not on HRA, and on transport allowance only in two narrow cases. State government employees follow their own orders and rates. Arrears are taxed in the year received. Check the final figure against your pay slip or with your Pay & Accounts Office.",
    "overview": "A DA calculator works out three things: your Dearness Allowance at the rate in force, what your pay looks like with DA, and the arrears when a rise is announced late. On the sample — basic pay ₹56,100, DA at 63% — the DA is ₹35,343 a month and ₹4,24,116 a year, the pay with DA is ₹91,443 a month, and the arrears for the 60% to 63% rise are ₹1,683 a month — ₹6,732 for the 4 months paid at the old rate. The Salary calculator works out the full pay packet; the Income Tax calculator shows the tax on the arrears. Everything is worked out in your browser; nothing is sent anywhere.",
