    "actNote": "The familiar 1961 numbers map to the Income-tax Act, 2025 from AY 2026-27 — the limits are unchanged: Section 24(b) becomes Section 22 (self-occupied interest under Section 22(2)(a), Rs.2,00,000, or Section 22(2)(b), Rs.30,000; let-out interest under Section 22(1)(b); the 30% standard deduction on rent under Section 22(1)(a); pre-construction interest in five equal instalments under Section 22(1)(c)); Section 80C becomes Section 123 with Schedule XV; Section 80EE becomes Section 130; Section 80EEA becomes Section 131; and Section 115BAC (the new regime) is replaced by the new Act's regime provisions. This page is framed for FY 2026-27 and uses the familiar 1961 numbers throughout, with the 2025 mapping noted here.",
    "checklist": [
      "Is the regime right — old or new? On the new regime a self-occupied home saves nothing, and the calculator must show Rs.0.",
      "Is the interest figure the year's interest — from the bank certificate or amortisation schedule — not the whole EMI?",
      "Is the 80C already used entered — EPF, PPF, ELSS, LIC and tuition fees — so the shared Rs.1,50,000 cap is not double-counted?",
      "Was construction completed within 5 years of borrowing? If not, the interest cap is Rs.30,000, not Rs.2,00,000.",
      "Is the extra benefit really available — the loan sanction date, the property value and first-time-buyer conditions all met?",
      "Is the property let out, with the annual rent entered? The let-out rules are different, and 80EE/80EEA add nothing there.",
      "Is the slab your marginal rate — the rate on your top slice of income — not your average rate?",
      "If the loan is joint, have you run the calculator on your share only, as a co-owner and co-borrower?",
      "Is the result an estimate — surcharge ignored, actual saving depends on your full income — and have you checked it with a chartered accountant before acting on it?"
    ],
