    "inputNote": "Pick how to calculate — the price of jewellery, the value of old gold, or how much gold a budget buys. For jewellery, enter the weight (in grams, tolas, sovereigns or 10-gram units), the purity (24K, 22K, 18K or 14K), and today's rate — the 24K rate per gram, or the rate for the chosen purity if that is what your jeweller quoted. Then the making charges (as a percentage of the gold value or a flat amount), the wastage percentage, any stone charges, and whether to add 3% GST. For old gold, enter the weight, the purity and the rate, and the buyback deduction (5% by default — the jeweller pays 95% of the pure gold value). For a budget, enter the amount and the purity. The sample — 20 g of 22K at Rs.11,500 a gram, 12% wastage, GST on — is filled in.",
    "key": "gpc",
    "kind": "gpc",
    "lead": "A gold bill is never just the weight times the rate. The jeweller adds wastage, making charges and stone charges, then 3% GST on the whole bill — and the rate itself moves every day. Enter the weight, the purity and today's rate, and see every line of the bill: the gold value, the wastage, the making, the stones, the GST split into CGST and SGST, and the true cost a gram. You can also value old gold for resale, or work out how much gold a budget buys. On the sample — 20 g of 22K at Rs.11,500 a gram, 12% wastage, 3% GST — the bill is Rs.2,65,328. Everything is worked out in your browser; nothing is sent anywhere.",
    "meta": "Gold price calculator — work out the price of gold jewellery with making charges, wastage and 3% GST, the value of your old gold, or how much gold your budget buys. Sample: 20 g of 22K at Rs.11,500 a gram is Rs.2,65,328 with 12% wastage and GST. Free, in your browser.",
    "methodology": "The rules and examples on this page were checked against sdev.in, calcnook.com, 5paisa.com, goldcalculator.net.in, goldmitra.in and zefince.com on 14 November 2026, and every worked example on the page reproduces its source exactly except where a convention difference is stated — see sources.md for the full list, including the 5paisa Rs.40 difference, the goldcalculator.net.in 22K Rs.9 difference and the zefince Rs.32 inconsistency. The calculator itself runs entirely in your browser: the gold-value, wastage, making, GST, buyback and budget arithmetic is the same code on the server-rendered page and in the live calculator. For related tools, the <a href=\"/gold-loan-calculator/\">Gold Loan EMI calculator</a> works out what you can borrow against the same gold, the <a href=\"/home-loan-emi-calculator/\">Home Loan EMI calculator</a> works out a loan EMI, and the <a href=\"/salary-calculator/\">Salary calculator</a> works out your monthly pay. The Income Tax Calculator works out the full year's tax on your whole income. Last updated 14 November 2026.",
