    "guideTitle": "How many months of cover, by household",
    "inputNote": "Enter your essential monthly expenses — what you must pay even if your income stops: rent or home loan EMI, groceries, utilities, insurance premiums, school fees, transport, medicines and other loan EMIs. Leave out holidays, eating out and investments you can pause. If you are not sure of the total, fill in the itemised breakdown below and it adds up into the total for you. Set the months of cover to the guidance for your household: 3 to 6 months for stable salaried income, 9 to 12 for irregular income or dependants. Enter what you have already saved, how much you can set aside each month, and how many months you want to take to build the rest. The sample — Rs.50,000 a month, 6 months, Rs.1,00,000 saved — is filled in.",
    "key": "efc",
