        "A fund of six months' salary sounds safe, but the fund has to pay your expenses, not replace your pay slip. If your essential expenses are Rs.50,000 and your salary is Rs.1,00,000, six months of salary is twice the fund you need — and six months of expenses on a Rs.40,000 salary is a fund you cannot build. Start from the expenses."
