    "starNote": "About the star rating: BEE's star labelling for room air conditioners rates a split AC by its ISEER \u2014 the Indian Seasonal Energy Efficiency Ratio. For January 2026 to December 2027 the bands are 3.50\u20133.79 for 1 star, 3.80\u20134.29 for 2 star, 4.30\u20134.99 for 3 star, 5.00\u20135.59 for 4 star, and 5.60 and above for 5 star (window ACs run lower, 2.90 to 3.70 and above). Those bands come from the gazette notifications S.O. 2794(E) of 16 July 2024 and S.O. 3984(E) of 28 August 2025, as reported by benchmarksutra.in \u2014 BEE's own star table could not be read directly on 14 November 2026, because beestarlabel.com serves a stale homepage with no table and the gazette PDF would not fetch. On the label's own annual-units figures, a 1.5-ton 5-star (ISEER 5.80) uses 681 units a year against 878 units for a 3-star (ISEER 4.50): about 22% fewer units. The often-quoted '5-star saves 20\u201325%' is not printed here as a BEE fact \u2014 it traces to a 2016 press report of a BEE claim of 20\u201322%, and the same study found 5-star units using more power above 40\u00b0C.",
