    "checklistTitle": "Before you trust the result",
    "cpwdNote": "About the CPWD benchmark: the Central Public Works Department publishes Plinth Area Rates for preliminary estimates of government buildings, and the 2025 edition (as on 1 April 2025) is the 12th since 1955. The figures on this page were verified from the official CPWD Plinth Area Rates 2025 document itself (hosted on ireps.gov.in): item 1.1.2, RCC-framed residential quarters with a 3.00 m floor height, Rs 24,410 per sqm; item 2.1, internal water supply and sanitary installations for quarters with attached toilets, +9% of the building cost; item 2.3, internal electric installations, +12.5% of the building cost. The document states that both percentages are percentages of the building cost, so they add: Rs 24,410 x (1 + 0.09 + 0.125) = Rs 29,658.15 per sqm, about Rs 2,755.33 per sq ft (1 sqm = 10.7639 sq ft) \u2014 which matches speakarch.com's printed Rs 29,658 per sqm and Rs 2,755 per sq ft exactly. Two things to keep in mind: CPWD publishes the rate for Delhi only, and it assumes government specifications and contracts. External service connections, local-body approvals and consultancy fees are extra in the CPWD rates too (items 2.2 and 3.0).",
