    "lead": "Enter the room size in feet, the doors and windows, the paint type and the number of coats — and get the litres to buy, the primer, the putty and the cost from your own per-litre prices.",
    "meta": "Paint calculator — work out how many litres of paint, primer and putty a room needs in India, from the room size in feet.",
    "methodology": "The rates on this page were checked against the calculators India actually uses, on 14 November 2026. All five were fetched in full: aapkapainter.com (worked examples, room table and coverage table), onsiteteams.com (working calculator, coverage table, primer and putty rates, worked example), calculatorking.in (working calculator in metres), bttotek.in (working calculator, worked example) and dailytools.in (working calculator, live result). Every worked example on the page reproduces its published figure exactly, except where a difference is stated: aapkapainter's room-table wall areas reproduce from the stated 21/13 sq ft deductions only for the small bedroom (360 − 60 = 300) and the hall (640 − 60 = 580) — the master bedroom's 420 sq ft (468 − 48) has no 21/13 combination, so the table's own wall areas are the source's figures and only its litres (area × 2 ÷ 120) are anchored; onsiteteams' worked example uses 12 sq ft per window (net 462, 6.6 litres, primer 2.77 litres) where this calculator uses 13 (net 459, 6.80 litres) and premium at its 135 midpoint rather than 140; onsiteteams' room table is approximate (marked ~) and its small-bedroom row implies no window deduction, so it is not anchored; the primer rate is onsiteteams' 150–200 (midpoint 175), where aapkapainter prints 80–100, bttotek 10–12 sq m/L (108–129 sq ft/L) and dailytools 6–8 sq m/L (65–86 sq ft/L); the putty rate is bttotek's 1.2 kg/m² for 2 coats, where onsiteteams and aapkapainter print 2–2.5 kg per 100 sq ft, roughly a fifth as much; and the putty formula in the first draft of this pack double-counted (area × 2 × 1.2 would give 240 kg for 100 sq m) — the shipped formula is area × 1.2, which reproduces bttotek's 120 kg exactly. This is a planning estimate, not a quotation: real use depends on wall roughness, porosity, colour change, application method and the tin's own stated rate; primer and putty figures are estimates; the cost comes only from the prices you enter; the ceiling is excluded unless you tick it; doors and windows use the standard 21/13 sq ft sizes — measure large openings. For related tools, the EMI Calculator works out the monthly cost of a loan, the Home Loan EMI Calculator covers a home loan, the SIP Calculator plans a monthly saving, the PPF Calculator and the FD Calculator plan the saving itself, the GST Calculator and the Percentage Calculator cover the arithmetic around a job, and the Income Tax Calculator covers the bigger money questions. Last updated 14 November 2026.",
