    "rateNote": "The third-party premium is the one part of the price no insurer controls: it is fixed by the regulator, by engine size, and identical everywhere. The 1-year rates have been in force since 1 June 2022. A new two-wheeler must by law take five years of third-party cover, paid upfront — and the five-year rate is NOT five times the annual rate (five years at ₹538 would be ₹2,690, but the published rate is ₹2,901). GST at 18% sits on top of each figure. Electric two-wheelers have their own kW-based rates (up to 3 kW ₹457, 3–7 kW ₹607, 7–16 kW ₹1,161, above 16 kW ₹2,383 a year), already including the 15% EV concession.",
