        "Multiply your body weight in kg by the rate for your goal: 0.83–1.0 g/kg for general health, 1.2–1.4 g/kg if you exercise regularly, 1.6–2.2 g/kg to build muscle or lose fat while keeping muscle, 1.0–1.2 g/kg if you are over 50, and 1.2–1.6 g/kg for endurance training. A 70 kg adult needs 58–70 g for general health, 84–98 g when active, and 112–154 g when building muscle."
