    "lead": "Enter your weight in kg, pick your goal, and get your daily protein target in grams — with the per-meal split, the ICMR RDA for your weight, and the calories it carries. Everything runs in your browser; nothing you type is sent or saved.",
    "meta": "Protein calculator — daily protein in grams for your weight and goal, with per-meal targets, the ICMR RDA (0.83 g/kg) and Indian food sources. General health 0.83–1.0, active 1.2–1.4, muscle 1.6–2.2 g/kg.",
    "methodology": "The arithmetic on this page was checked against the five protein calculators people actually use, on 15 November 2026. All five were fetched in full: FitTrackPro's Protein Calculator (ICMR–NIN 2020/2024 RDA 0.83 g/kg; table for 50–100 kg — general health 42 g at 50 kg, 50 g at 60 kg, 54 g at 65 kg, 58 g at 70 kg, 66 g at 80 kg, 83 g at 100 kg; active 1.2–1.4 g/kg; muscle and fat loss 1.6–2.2 g/kg — every row reproduces exactly; older adults 1.0–1.2 g/kg; Morton et al. 2018, plateau around 1.62 g/kg to 2.2; its food table carries no source citation for every row, so the food figures on this page are the cross-checked ones, not IFCT 2017 values); CalcVind's Protein Calculator (worked example: 70 kg, regular exercise, 3 meals — 77–98 g a day, 26–33 g a meal; the top of the range reproduces, the bottom does NOT: its lower bound is 1.1 g/kg, not 1.2; its food table — chicken breast 31 g per 100 g, paneer 18 g, soya chunks 26 g per 50 g dry, eggs 12 g for 2, fish rohu 20 g per 100 g, dal 9 g a katori, chana/rajma 11 g, curd 7 g a cup, milk 8 g a glass, peanuts 8 g per 30 g — agrees with the other sources and is the basis of the food table here; sources: ISSN position stand 2017 and ICMR–NIN 2020; it also prints 0.8 g/kg as the general-health lower bound and 'up to 2.4 g/kg' for fat loss, both of which differ from this page and are stated); FitLives' Protein Calculator (70 kg: general health 1.2 g/kg → 84 g, fat loss 1.8 → 126 g, muscle 2.0 → 140 g — the two higher points sit inside this page's ranges; the 84 g point does NOT sit in this page's general-health range, because FitLives' general health includes light activity at 1.2 g/kg, which is this page's active range; worked examples Priya 60 kg fat loss 108 g a day, range 96–120 g, about 36 g a meal, and Rahul 75 kg muscle 150 g a day, range 135–165 g, about 38 g across 4 meals — the points and per-meal figures sit inside this page's ranges, while the ranges themselves are ±0.2 g/kg around a point and this page uses the full goal ranges; sources: ISSN 2017, Morton et al. 2018, Helms et al. 2014, Schoenfeld & Aragon 2018, ICMR–NIN 2020); MuscleBlaze's How to Calculate Your Protein Intake (worked examples: 65 kg woman × 1.2 = 78 g, 80 kg man × 1.8 = 144 g — both sit inside this page's ranges; ICMR–NIN 2020 RDA 0.83 g/kg and EAR 0.66 g/kg; cereal-based diets around 1 g/kg; at least 66% of protein from quality sources; older adults 1.0–1.2 g/kg; muscle 1.6–2.0 g/kg — this page runs to 2.2 g/kg per Morton et al. 2018; NSO Report No. 594, 2025 — Indian diets derive close to 60% of protein from cereals); and ProteinIntakeCalculator (goal ranges general 0.8–1.0, fat loss 1.2–1.4, muscle 1.6–2.2, endurance 1.2–1.6, strength 1.6–2.0, older adult 1.0–1.2 — its fat-loss range and its 0.8 lower bound both differ from this page and are stated; worked example 75 kg at 20% body fat, muscle building — lean mass 60 kg → 96–132 g a day, 24–33 g across 4 meals — does NOT reproduce on total weight: this page gives 120–165 g a day, 30–41 g a meal; ICMR reference man 65 kg → 54 g and reference woman 55 kg → 46 g, both reproduce exactly; its food table — chicken breast 31 g, paneer 18 g, egg 13 g, lentils/dal 9 g, tofu 8 g per 100 g — agrees with the other sources). The official anchor is ICMR–National Institute of Nutrition, Nutrient Requirements for Indians (2020): RDA 0.83 g/kg/day, EAR 0.66 g/kg/day. This is an estimate, not medical advice: if you have kidney disease, ask your doctor first; if you are pregnant or breastfeeding, follow your doctor's advice. No prices on this page are market fact — there are no prices on this page at all. For related tools, the BMI Calculator works out your body mass index from your height and weight. Last updated 15 November 2026.",
