    "inputNote": "The sample is a 12 × 15 ft room (180 sq ft) with a flat gypsum ceiling in a Tier-2 city — ₹18,000 typically (₹12,600–₹23,400), or ₹100 a sq ft. IdeasAndLiving's worked example gives the same base: 180 sq ft of gypsum at ₹100 a sq ft is ₹18,000.",
    "key": "falseCeilingCalculator",
    "kind": "falseCeilingCalculator",
    "lead": "Enter the room size and pick the ceiling type and design, and get a low–typical–high cost range for Indian 2026 rates — with cove and profile lighting, finishing, the city difference and GST as separate line items. Or switch to the material BOQ and count the boards, channels, screws and lights for the same room. Everything runs in your browser; nothing you type is sent or saved.",
    "meta": "False ceiling cost calculator — POP, gypsum, grid and PVC rates per sq ft, cove and profile lighting, city-wise cost and a gypsum/POP material BOQ for Indian homes. Indicative 2026 ranges.",
    "methodology": "The arithmetic on this page was checked against the five false-ceiling calculators and guides India actually uses, on 15 November 2026. All five were fetched in full: InteriorCalculator's False Ceiling Cost Calculator (2026) (per-sq-ft rates POP ₹55–90, gypsum ₹70–130, grid ₹60–100, PVC ₹85–140; cove LED ₹120–200 per Rft of cove run, cove run ~30% of the perimeter; profile lighting ₹2,500–5,000 per metre; finishing ₹35–60 per sq ft; city table for a 200 sq ft gypsum ceiling with cove lighting — Mumbai ₹35,000–60,000, Delhi NCR ₹32,000–55,000, Bengaluru ₹28,000–52,000, Hyderabad/Chennai/Pune ₹26,000–50,000, Tier-2 ₹22,000–45,000; area slider 40–1,200 sq ft); Toolique's False Ceiling Calculator (effective-area multipliers flat ×1.00, single cove tray ×1.20, floating island ×1.35, designer ×1.60; single rates gypsum ₹105, POP ₹130, PVC ₹85, WPC ₹260, grid ₹75, aluminium baffle ₹380 per sq ft; FAQ ranges gypsum ₹95–135, POP ₹115–165, PVC ₹75–105, WPC ₹240–340, grid ₹65–90; GI framing per IS 2095 — perimeter channels 610 mm, ceiling sections 457 mm c/c, intermediate channels 1,220 mm c/c, screws 200 mm along board edges; downlights 1 per 20–25 sq ft; 150 W driver per 45–55 Rft of cove LED); Kalikolom's Drop Ceiling Cost Calculator (a 12 × 14 ft room, 168 sq ft, with standard 2 × 2 ft tiles comes to about ₹18,204 installed, ₹108 per sq ft, and ₹14,004 for materials only; India grid/mineral-fibre ceilings roughly ₹85–150 per sq ft installed — a grid/tile drop ceiling, a different system from gypsum/POP); IdeasAndLiving's false ceiling cost guide (worked example: 12 × 15 ft = 180 sq ft, gypsum at ₹100 per sq ft → ₹18,000, plus ₹5,000 of lighting and ₹3,000 of borders = ₹26,000); and SpaceForm's False Ceiling Cost Calculator (plain single-level gypsum or POP ₹85–130 per sq ft installed, standard designs with cove lighting ₹110–170, designer multi-level ₹170–300+ per sq ft). The joint-compound allowance (0.06 kg per sq ft for 3 coats) comes from USG's SHEETROCK all-purpose joint compound specification (125–150 lb per 1,000 sq ft, i.e. 0.057–0.068 kg per sq ft). The city multipliers are this page's own derivation: the midpoint of each city's published range divided by the Tier-2 midpoint (Mumbai 47,500 ÷ 33,500 = 1.42, Delhi NCR 43,500 ÷ 33,500 = 1.30, Bengaluru 40,000 ÷ 33,500 = 1.19, Hyderabad/Chennai/Pune 38,000 ÷ 33,500 = 1.13, Tier-2 1.00). The screw count (37 per board) is this page's estimating assumption from Toolique's 200 mm spacing along a 7.32 m board perimeter, with shared edges counted per board, so it is conservative. For related tools, the CGPA Calculator converts CGPA to percentage, the BMI Calculator works out body mass index, the EMI Calculator works out any loan's monthly payment, the Home Loan EMI Calculator works out the monthly cost of a home loan, the Compound Interest Calculator and SIP Calculator cover savings growth, the PPF Calculator covers the Public Provident Fund, the Percentage Calculator and GST Calculator cover everyday percentages and tax, and the Income Tax Calculator covers tax. Last updated 15 November 2026.",
