    "mistakesTitle": "Common false-ceiling mistakes to avoid",
    "modelNote": "The arithmetic on this page was checked against the five false-ceiling calculators India actually uses. The ceiling cost is the effective area (flat area × the design multiplier: flat ×1.00, single cove tray ×1.20, floating island ×1.35, designer ×1.60) times the material rate, as a low–typical–high range (POP ₹55–90, gypsum ₹70–130, grid ₹60–100, PVC ₹85–140 per sq ft; typical = midpoint). Cove lighting is the cove run (30% of the room perimeter) at ₹120–₹200 per Rft; profile lighting is ₹2,500–₹5,000 a metre; finishing is ₹35–₹60 a sq ft of effective area; extras are rupees you enter, added after the city multiplier. City multipliers are the midpoint ratios of InteriorCalculator's 200 sq ft gypsum-with-cove table against Tier-2 (Mumbai ×1.42, Delhi NCR ×1.30, Bengaluru ×1.19, Hyderabad/Chennai/Pune ×1.13, Tier-2 ×1.00). GST is 18%, off by default. The BOQ counts gypsum boards (4 ft × 8 ft, +10% wastage), perimeter channel (the room perimeter), ceiling sections at 457 mm centres and intermediate channels at 1,220 mm centres to IS 2095, screws at 200 mm centres (37 a board), joint compound at 0.06 kg a sq ft for 3 coats, downlights at 1 per 20–25 sq ft and one 150 W driver per 45–55 Rft of cove LED. Published figures that do NOT reproduce on this page are shown with the reason: Toolique's POP single rate of ₹130 sits above InteriorCalculator's ₹55–₹90 plain-POP range, because Toolique prices a premium hand-troweled POP; and Kalikolom's 168 sq ft grid/tile drop ceiling at ₹18,204 (₹108 a sq ft) sits above this page's grid range, because Kalikolom prices a tile-and-grid system with mineral-fibre tiles — a different system, priced per tile.",
    "notice": "Indicative 2026 range — not a quote. No fixed price is printed on this page as fact: every rate is a published range with its source and date.",
    "overview": "It turns a room size into a cost range for a false ceiling — or into the boards, channels, screws and lights to order for the same room. A 12 × 15 ft room (180 sq ft) with a flat gypsum ceiling in a Tier-2 city costs ₹18,000 typically (₹12,600–₹23,400), or ₹100 a sq ft — the same base IdeasAndLiving prints for its worked example. The same room with a single cove tray is ₹24,192, and a 200 sq ft gypsum ceiling with cove lighting is ₹38,170 in Mumbai and ₹26,880 in a Tier-2 city, both inside InteriorCalculator's published city ranges. In the second mode it counts the material: 7 gypsum boards, 54 ft of perimeter channel, 132.0 ft of ceiling sections, 259 screws and 10.8 kg of joint compound for the flat 180 sq ft ceiling, with 7–9 downlights. It is an estimate for planning and ordering, not a quote — and where the published calculators disagree, this page prints the difference with the reason instead of silently following one of them.",
    "overviewTitle": "What does a false ceiling cost calculator do?",
