    "rateTitle": "False ceiling rates per sq ft in India (2026)",
    "rulesNote": "Seven rules, each one checkable against the sources. Nothing here is a guess — and where the sources disagree, the page says so.",
    "rulesRows": [
      {
        "detail": "Effective area = flat area × the design multiplier. Toolique's rule: flat single level ×1.00, single cove tray (4–6 in drop) ×1.20, floating island double tier ×1.35, designer CNC/curves ×1.60. The extra is the vertical drop fascia — a cove tray adds 20% of area before a rupee of lighting is counted.",
        "rule": "The design multiplies the area, not just the price"
      },
      {
        "detail": "InteriorCalculator's 2026 rates are ranges, not prices: POP ₹55–90, gypsum ₹70–130, grid ₹60–100, PVC ₹85–140 per sq ft. This page's typical is the midpoint of each range (gypsum ₹100, POP ₹72.50, grid ₹80, PVC ₹112.50). Toolique's single rates sit inside these ranges for gypsum (₹105), PVC (₹85) and grid (₹75) — only POP (₹130) sits above, because Toolique prices a premium hand-troweled POP.",
        "rule": "The rate is a range; the typical is the midpoint"
      },
      {
        "detail": "Cove lighting is priced against ~30% of the room perimeter — InteriorCalculator's rule for the typical run of a living-room cove — at ₹120–₹200 per Rft. For a 12 × 15 ft room the perimeter is 54 ft, the cove run is 16.2 Rft and the cove costs ₹2,592 typically. One 150 W SMPS driver is needed per 45–55 Rft of cove LED (Toolique).",
        "rule": "Cove lighting runs 30% of the perimeter"
      },
      {
        "detail": "The city multipliers are this page's own derivation from InteriorCalculator's 200 sq ft gypsum-with-cove table: the midpoint of each city's published range divided by the Tier-2 midpoint (₹33,500). Mumbai ₹47,500 ÷ ₹33,500 = 1.42, Delhi NCR ₹43,500 ÷ ₹33,500 = 1.30, Bengaluru ₹40,000 ÷ ₹33,500 = 1.19, Hyderabad/Chennai/Pune ₹38,000 ÷ ₹33,500 = 1.13, Tier-2 ×1.00. Every city's typical on this page falls inside its published range.",
        "rule": "City multipliers are midpoint ratios, not guesses"
      },
      {
        "detail": "The published ranges do not all say whether GST is included. Kalikolom notes many quotes exclude GST, wiring and lights, and SpaceForm's bands exclude designer fees. So this calculator leaves GST off by default and adds 18% only if you switch it on — the page never silently adds tax to a rate that may already include it.",
        "rule": "GST is off by default — the sources disagree"
      },
      {
        "detail": "GI framing to IS 2095, as Toolique states it: perimeter channels fixed at 610 mm intervals along the walls, ceiling sections spaced at 457 mm centre-to-centre, intermediate channels at 1,220 mm centre-to-centre, connecting clips and drywall screws at 200 mm along board edges, and joint compound in 3 expanding coats with 50 mm fibre/paper joint tape. Boards are 4 ft × 8 ft (32 sq ft) with 10% wastage.",
        "rule": "The BOQ follows IS 2095 framing rules"
      },
      {
        "detail": "Downlights: 1 recessed LED downlight (9–12 W) for every 20–25 sq ft of ceiling area (Toolique) — so a 180 sq ft room needs 7–9 and a 200 sq ft room needs 8–10, shown as a range. Cove LED: one 150 W constant-voltage SMPS driver per 45–55 Rft, for high-density 240 LED/m strips at ~12 W/m. Joint compound: 0.06 kg per sq ft for 3 coats, from USG's SHEETROCK specification (125–150 lb per 1,000 sq ft).",
        "rule": "Lights and compound have published rules too"
      }
    ],
    "rulesTitle": "The rules behind the answer",
