    "mistakesTitle": "Common modular-kitchen mistakes to avoid",
    "modelNote": "The arithmetic on this page was checked against the five modular-kitchen calculators India actually uses. The cabinet cost is the kitchen area times the layout rate (Livspace, 2026: straight ₹2,500–3,500, L-shaped ₹2,800–4,000, parallel ₹2,600–4,000, U-shaped ₹3,000–4,200 per sq ft; island ₹3,500–5,000 is this page's stated estimate) times the finish multiplier (laminate ×1.00, membrane ×1.15, acrylic ×1.35, PU ×1.60, veneer ×1.75, solid wood ×2.20) times the carcass multiplier (MDF ×1.00, HDHMR ×1.08, BWP plywood ×1.12), as a low–typical–high range with the typical at the midpoint. Installation is 10% of the cabinet cost — a split of the all-in layout rate for the breakup, not an addition. The countertop is the counter run (straight = length, L-shaped = length + width, parallel = 2 × length, U-shaped = 2 × length + width, island = 2 × length + width + 6 ft for the island run) × 2 ft deep, at granite ₹250–450, quartz ₹450–1,000 or marble ₹700–1,400 per sq ft (marble is a planning estimate — no published marble rate was found). Hardware is priced per sq ft (standard in the rate, soft-close + pull-outs ₹200–300, premium ₹400–600) and a tall unit / pantry is ₹18,000–₹60,000. City multipliers come from NoBroker's city table (metro ×1.28, Tier-2 ×1.00, Tier-3 ×0.83). GST is 18%, off by default. Published figures that do NOT reproduce on this page are shown with the reason: Asian Paints' material-only laminate rate (₹700–₹1,200 a sq ft) sits far below the all-in rates, because it is shutter-only; Novella's quartz uplift (₹30,000–₹60,000) is for larger Gurgaon luxury kitchens, above this page's ₹13,500 for a standard kitchen; Novella's base-luxury lump sums state no size and cannot be reproduced from a per-sq-ft rate; and NoBroker's overall ₹1,800–₹4,500 a sq ft covers standard layouts and finishes, not an island kitchen in solid wood with marble and premium hardware.",
    "notice": "Indicative 2026 range — not a quote. No fixed price is printed on this page as fact: every rate is a published range with its source and date.",
    "overview": "It turns a kitchen size into a cost range for a modular kitchen — cabinets, countertop, hardware, tall unit, city and GST as separate line items. A 10 × 8 ft kitchen (80 sq ft), L-shaped, laminate on MDF with a granite countertop in a Tier-2 city costs ₹2,84,600 typically (₹2,33,000–₹3,36,200), or ₹3,558 a sq ft — inside Livspace's L-shaped band of ₹2–3.5 lakh and Asian Paints' ₹2,500–₹4,000 average. The same kitchen in acrylic is ₹3,79,800, in PU ₹4,47,800, and with a quartz countertop ₹2,98,100. Interior Company's three packages land within 5% of this page's nearest matches — Silver ₹4,044 against ₹4,068, Gold ₹4,575 against ₹4,380, Platinum ₹5,136 against ₹5,283 a sq ft. It is an estimate for planning and comparing quotes, not a quote — and where the published calculators disagree, this page prints the difference with the reason instead of silently following one of them.",
