  "rateTitle": "What does each level pay? Six levels at the current DA",
  "rulesNote": "Eight rules, each one checkable against the official sources. Nothing here is a guess \u2014 and where the sources define a figure differently, the page says so.",
  "rulesRows": [
    {
      "detail": "The first cell of each level in the CCS (Revised Pay) Rules, 2016, Part A of the Schedule as substituted by G.S.R. 592(E) dated 15 June 2017: Level 1 \u20b918,000, Level 2 \u20b919,900, Level 3 \u20b921,700, Level 4 \u20b925,500, Level 5 \u20b929,200, Level 6 \u20b935,400, Level 7 \u20b944,900, Level 8 \u20b947,600, Level 9 \u20b953,100, Level 10 \u20b956,100, Level 11 \u20b967,700, Level 12 \u20b978,800, Level 13 \u20b91,23,100 (amended from \u20b91,18,500), Level 13A \u20b91,31,100, Level 14 \u20b91,44,200, Level 15 \u20b91,82,200, Level 16 \u20b92,05,400, Level 17 \u20b92,25,000, Level 18 \u20b92,50,000 (a single fixed cell).",
      "rule": "Basic pay comes from the pay matrix"
    },
    {
      "detail": "DA is a percentage of basic pay, revised twice a year. The current rate is 63% from 1 July 2026 (PIB Release ID 2329484, 28 Oct 2026), up from 60% from 1 January 2026. On the sample, 44,900 \u00d7 0.63 = \u20b928,287. The rate is an editable input on the form.",
      "rule": "DA is 63% of basic pay from 1 July 2026"
    },
    {
      "detail": "HRA is a percentage of basic pay by city class, or the floor, whichever is higher. The rates are 24%/16%/8% (X/Y/Z) when DA is below 25%, 27%/18%/9% from 25% DA, and 30%/20%/10% from 50% DA; the floors are \u20b95,400/\u20b93,600/\u20b91,800 (DoE OM No. 2/5/2017-E.II(B), 7 July 2017). At 63% DA the 30%/20%/10% tier applies. No HRA is paid in government quarters.",
      "rule": "HRA follows the city class and the DA tier"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Transport allowance is a fixed slab by level and city, plus DA on the slab (DoE OM No. 21/5/2017-E.II(B), 7 July 2017): Levels 9+ \u20b97,200/\u20b93,600, Levels 3\u20138 \u20b93,600/\u20b91,800, Levels 1\u20132 \u20b91,350/\u20b9900 (higher-TPTA cities / other places). On the sample, the Level 7 slab is \u20b93,600 and DA adds \u20b92,268, so \u20b95,868. The Level 1\u20132 exception for basic pay of \u20b924,200 or more is not modelled.",
      "rule": "Transport allowance is a slab plus DA"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Under NPS, 10% of (basic + DA) is deducted from the employee and the government adds 14% (MoF Gazette Notification F. No. 1/3/2016-PR dated 31 Jan 2019, in force 1 Apr 2019). On the sample that is \u20b97,319 deducted and \u20b910,246 added. NPS is compulsory for employees who joined on or after 1 January 2004; GPF employees have no NPS deduction.",
      "rule": "NPS is 10% from the employee, 14% from the government"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The CGHS contribution is fixed by level: \u20b9250 a month for Levels 1\u20135, \u20b9450 for Level 6, \u20b9650 for Levels 7\u201311 and \u20b91,000 for Level 12 and above (MoHFW OM dated 9 Jan 2017, in force 1 Feb 2017, reaffirmed 28 June 2024). It is a flat deduction \u2014 it does not depend on basic pay.",
      "rule": "CGHS is a fixed monthly contribution by level"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Income tax follows the new regime for FY 2026-27 (incometax.gov.in, AY 2027-28): nil to \u20b94 lakh, 5% to \u20b98 lakh, 10% to \u20b912 lakh, 15% to \u20b916 lakh, 20% to \u20b920 lakh, 25% to \u20b924 lakh, 30% above \u20b924 lakh, plus 4% cess. The \u20b975,000 standard deduction comes off first, and the Section 87A rebate (up to \u20b960,000) wipes out the tax when taxable income is \u20b912 lakh or less, with marginal relief just above. Surcharge applies above \u20b950 lakh. The employer's NPS share is not deducted, following the site's own Income Tax Calculator.",
      "rule": "Income tax is the new regime with the 87A rebate"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The annual increment is 3% of basic pay, taken as the next cell down in the same level: basic \u00d7 1.03, rounded to the nearest \u20b9100 (Rule 10, CCS (Revised Pay) Rules, 2016). One increment a year, on 1 January or 1 July. Promotion moves to the next level's first cell. Level 18 has no increment or promotion \u2014 \u20b92,50,000 is a single fixed cell.",
      "rule": "The increment is 3%, the promotion is the next level's first cell"
    }
  ],
