  "mistakesTitle": "Common 8th Pay Commission mistakes to avoid",
  "modelNote": "The arithmetic on this page is exact, with round-half-up (1e-9 nudge), as in the 375 pure file. Projected basic pay = current basic \u00d7 fitment factor, rounded to the nearest \u20b910 (half-up). DA = projected basic \u00d7 DA rate, rounded to the rupee; the DA rate defaults to 0% because DA restarts at 0% after the revision. HRA = projected basic \u00d7 the current 30%/20%/10% rate for the city class (a stated projection assumption \u2014 the revised rates have not been notified), or the floor (\u20b95,400 X, \u20b93,600 Y, \u20b91,800 Z), whichever is higher; no HRA when the city class is none. Transport allowance = the slab for the level and city (Levels 9+: \u20b97,200/\u20b93,600; Levels 3\u20138: \u20b93,600/\u20b91,800; Levels 1\u20132: \u20b91,350/\u20b9900) plus DA on the slab. Gross monthly = projected basic + DA + HRA + TA; gross annual = gross monthly \u00d7 12. NPS employee share = 10% of (projected basic + DA) on NPS, \u20b90 on GPF; government share = 14% of (projected basic + DA) on NPS, shown for information. CGHS = \u20b9250 (Levels 1\u20135), \u20b9450 (Level 6), \u20b9650 (Levels 7\u201311), \u20b91,000 (Level 12+). Taxable income = gross annual \u2212 \u20b975,000 standard deduction, floored at \u20b90. Income tax follows the new regime for FY 2026-27 (AY 2027-28): nil to \u20b94 lakh, 5% to \u20b98 lakh, 10% to \u20b912 lakh, 15% to \u20b916 lakh, 20% to \u20b920 lakh, 25% to \u20b924 lakh, 30% above, with the Section 87A rebate up to \u20b960,000 when taxable income is \u20b912 lakh or less, marginal relief just above \u20b912 lakh, surcharge above \u20b950 lakh and 4% cess. Net monthly = gross monthly \u2212 NPS \u2212 CGHS \u2212 professional tax \u2212 income tax \u00f7 12. Today's gross and net are computed with the same inputs under the 7th Pay Commission (current basic, DA 63%, HRA 30/20/10 with minimums, TA with DA 63%); the increase is the projected figure minus today's, in rupees and as a percentage.",
  "notice": "An estimate, not the new pay. No fitment factor or pay matrix has been notified \u2014 the figures on this page are projections at the fitment factor you choose, and they change if the Commission recommends otherwise. The HRA rates after the revision have not been notified either: the tool applies the current 30%/20%/10% tiers as a stated assumption. DA restarts at 0% on the form \u2014 raise it to model a post-implementation DA rate. The Level 1\u20132 transport allowance exception (\u20b924,200+ basic) and the Level 14+ official-car transport allowance option are not modelled. CGEGIS is not deducted because the pay-level to group mapping is not officially verified. Income tax is an estimate under the new regime for FY 2026-27; the Income Tax Calculator gives the exact figure for a salary you already know.",
  "overview": "It projects the 8th Pay Commission pay slip for a central government employee at the fitment factor you choose: the projected basic pay (current basic \u00d7 fitment, rounded to the nearest \u20b910), dearness allowance restarting at 0%, house rent allowance by city class, transport allowance by level and city, NPS and CGHS deductions, new-regime income tax, and the in-hand pay \u2014 plus the increase over today's 7th Pay Commission pay slip. On the sample \u2014 Level 7, \u20b944,900 basic, X city, fitment 2.57 \u2014 the projected basic is \u20b91,15,390, the gross is \u20b91,53,607 a month, deductions are \u20b925,505.92 and the net is \u20b91,28,101.08 a month: \u20b961,082 a month more than today's \u20b992,525 gross. Nothing here is official: no fitment factor and no pay matrix has been notified, so every figure is a projection. This is a different job from any other calculator on the site: the 7th Pay Commission Salary Calculator works out the pay slip you are actually paid today.",
  "overviewTitle": "What does an 8th Pay Commission salary calculator do?",
