  "rulesRows": [
    {
      "detail": "The first cell of each level in the CCS (Revised Pay) Rules, 2016, Part A of the Schedule as substituted by G.S.R. 592(E) dated 15 June 2017: Level 1 \u20b918,000, Level 2 \u20b919,900, Level 3 \u20b921,700, Level 4 \u20b925,500, Level 5 \u20b929,200, Level 6 \u20b935,400, Level 7 \u20b944,900, Level 8 \u20b947,600, Level 9 \u20b953,100, Level 10 \u20b956,100, Level 11 \u20b967,700, Level 12 \u20b978,800, Level 13 \u20b91,23,100 (amended from \u20b91,18,500), Level 13A \u20b91,31,100, Level 14 \u20b91,44,200, Level 15 \u20b91,82,200, Level 16 \u20b92,05,400, Level 17 \u20b92,25,000, Level 18 \u20b92,50,000 (a single fixed cell).",
      "rule": "Basic pay comes from the pay matrix"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Projected basic pay = current basic \u00d7 fitment factor, rounded to the nearest \u20b910 (half-up). On the sample, 44,900 \u00d7 2.57 = 1,15,393 \u2192 \u20b91,15,390. On a \u20b935,400 basic at 1.92 the product is \u20b967,968 \u2192 \u20b967,970. The rounding convention is stated on the page.",
      "rule": "Projected basic is basic \u00d7 fitment, rounded to \u20b910"
    },
    {
      "detail": "No fitment factor has been notified as of 16 November 2026. The scenarios on the page are media-reported: 1.92 is the widely reported consensus projection (Kotak ~1.8, Ambit 1.83\u20132.46), 2.57 is the 7th Pay Commission's factor, 2.86 is the reported upper end of a 2.28\u20132.86 range, and 3.83 is a staff-side demand from the NC-JCM memorandum of April 2026 (a \u20b969,000 minimum basic, 3.833 \u00d7 \u20b918,000). The tool defaults to 2.57 and accepts any factor from 1.00 to 4.00.",
      "rule": "The fitment factor is a scenario, not a decision"
    },
    {
      "detail": "DA restarts at 0% after the revision, because the fitment factor absorbs the DA already being paid: a factor of 1.63 folds the current 63% DA into the new basic pay. That is the pattern the 7th Pay Commission followed (its 2.57 factor absorbed 125% DA plus a real rise of about 14%), and it is what every 8th Pay Commission calculator assumes \u2014 but it has not been notified, so the DA rate is an editable input on the form. DA is then projected basic \u00d7 DA rate, rounded to the rupee.",
      "rule": "DA restarts at 0% after the revision"
    },
    {
      "detail": "HRA is projected basic \u00d7 the HRA rate for the city class, or the floor, whichever is higher. The tool applies the current 30%/20%/10% tiers (X/Y/Z) and the floors \u20b95,400/\u20b93,600/\u20b91,800 from DoE OM No. 2/5/2017-E.II(B), 7 July 2017, as a stated projection assumption \u2014 the HRA rates after the revision have NOT been notified. No HRA is paid in government quarters.",
      "rule": "HRA follows the city class \u2014 a stated assumption"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Transport allowance is a fixed slab by level and city, plus DA on the slab (DoE OM No. 21/5/2017-E.II(B), 7 July 2017): Levels 9+ \u20b97,200/\u20b93,600, Levels 3\u20138 \u20b93,600/\u20b91,800, Levels 1\u20132 \u20b91,350/\u20b9900 (higher-TPTA cities / other places). On the sample, the Level 7 slab is \u20b93,600 and DA adds \u20b90 at 0% DA (\u20b9180 at 5% DA). The Level 1\u20132 exception for basic pay of \u20b924,200 or more is not modelled.",
      "rule": "Transport allowance is a slab plus DA"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Under NPS, 10% of (projected basic + DA) is deducted from the employee and the government adds 14% (MoF Gazette Notification F. No. 1/3/2016-PR dated 31 Jan 2019, in force 1 Apr 2019). On the sample that is \u20b911,539 deducted and \u20b916,155 added. NPS is compulsory for employees who joined on or after 1 January 2004; GPF employees have no NPS deduction. The CGHS contribution is fixed by level: \u20b9250 a month for Levels 1\u20135, \u20b9450 for Level 6, \u20b9650 for Levels 7\u201311 and \u20b91,000 for Level 12 and above (MoHFW OM dated 9 Jan 2017, in force 1 Feb 2017, reaffirmed 28 June 2024).",
      "rule": "NPS is 10% from the employee, 14% from the government; CGHS is fixed by level"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Income tax follows the new regime for FY 2026-27 (AY 2027-28, incometax.gov.in): nil to \u20b94 lakh, 5% to \u20b98 lakh, 10% to \u20b912 lakh, 15% to \u20b916 lakh, 20% to \u20b920 lakh, 25% to \u20b924 lakh, 30% above \u20b924 lakh, plus 4% cess. The \u20b975,000 standard deduction comes off first, and the Section 87A rebate (up to \u20b960,000) wipes out the tax when taxable income is \u20b912 lakh or less, with marginal relief just above. Surcharge applies above \u20b950 lakh. On the sample, taxable income is \u20b917,68,284 and tax is \u20b91,59,803 a year. The employer's NPS share is not deducted, following the site's own Income Tax Calculator.",
      "rule": "Income tax is the new regime with the 87A rebate"
    }
  ],
