  "distinction": "The Personal Loan EMI Calculator works out the EMI on a loan taken by an individual, from income and a credit score. This tool is for a business: the loan types are business schemes (term, Mudra, CGTMSE-backed, machinery, working capital), the rates are business-loan rates (indicative 13.50% and up, November 2026), the tenures run to 10 years, the processing fee comes with 18% GST, and the interest is a business expense that reduces taxable profit. The Home Loan EMI Calculator is for a home loan, secured by the house, over up to 30 years, with tax benefits under different sections. The Car Loan EMI Calculator, Education Loan EMI Calculator, Bike Loan EMI Calculator and Gold Loan Calculator are for a car, an education, a bike and a gold-backed loan \u2014 different collateral, different rates and tenures, and the interest is not a business expense. The Credit Card EMI Calculator is for converting card spends into instalments, at card rates. The formula is the same reducing-balance EMI everywhere \u2014 P \u00d7 r \u00d7 (1+r)^n \u00f7 ((1+r)^n \u2212 1) \u2014 but the audience, the rates, the tenures, the fees, the tax treatment and the schemes are different, and so is the answer.",
