  "mistakesTitle": "Common business loan EMI mistakes to avoid",
  "modelNote": "The arithmetic on this page is exact, with round-half-up (1e-9 nudge), as in the 377 pure file. EMI = P \u00d7 r \u00d7 (1+r)^n \u00f7 ((1+r)^n \u2212 1), with r = annual rate / 1200 and n = tenure in months, to 2 decimals. Total payable = EMI \u00d7 tenure, rounded to the rupee; total interest = total payable \u2212 loan amount. Processing fee = loan amount \u00d7 fee%, rounded to the rupee; GST on the fee = fee \u00d7 18%, rounded to the rupee; amount disbursed = loan amount \u2212 fee \u2212 GST; effective cost = total interest + fee + GST. EMI per \u20b91 lakh = the EMI on \u20b91,00,000 at the same rate and tenure, to 2 decimals. First-year interest, principal and balance are the first 12 months (or the whole tenure if shorter) of the amortisation schedule, month by month at the reducing balance, each rounded to the rupee. Loan type fills typical rate, tenure and fee and shows the scheme note; it does not change the EMI maths. A Mudra amount above \u20b920 lakh is flagged (mudraOverLimit), not silently accepted. Rate bands are indicative (November 2026), never quotes.",
  "notice": "An estimate, not a quote. The EMI is worked out from the figures you type \u2014 the rate you are offered depends on your business, turnover, credit history and the lender's policy, and the processing fee varies by lender. The rate bands on this page are indicative (November 2026), never quotes. The interest on a business loan is a business expense \u2014 the tax illustration on this page is a general point at a stated slab, not advice for your business. This is not financial advice.",
  "overview": "It works out the monthly EMI, total interest and total payable on a business loan \u2014 plus the processing fee with 18% GST, the amount actually disbursed and the effective cost of borrowing. On the sample \u2014 a term loan of \u20b910,00,000 at 14% a year over 60 months with a 1% processing fee \u2014 the EMI is \u20b923,268.25 a month, the total interest is \u20b93,96,095, and \u20b99,88,200 is disbursed. Pick a loan type and the typical rate, tenure and fee fill themselves in: Mudra (PMMY) at 11% over 60 months, CGTMSE-backed at 13%, machinery at 13.5% over 84 months, working capital at 15% over 12 months. The page also shows the EMI per \u20b91 lakh for quick comparisons and the first year of the amortisation schedule. Nothing here is a quote: the lender's own business, turnover, credit-history and collateral checks decide the sanction and the rate. This is a different job from any other EMI calculator on the site: the Personal Loan EMI Calculator is for an individual's loan, the Home Loan EMI Calculator for a house, and the rest for a car, an education, a bike, gold or card spends \u2014 this one is for a business, with business schemes, business rates, fees with GST, and interest that is a business expense.",
