    "factorTitle": "Every figure on the sample, and how it is worked out",
    "faq": [
      [
        "How much do packers and movers charge in India?",
        "It depends on the home size and the distance. A 2 BHK within a city is about ₹6,500–₹16,000 before GST (InteriorCalculator), and ₹7,670–₹16,520 with 18% GST on this tool's range. A 1 BHK within a city is ₹4,550–₹8,000 before GST. A 2 BHK over 300–1,000 km is ₹18,000–₹35,000 before GST. These are planning ranges from published mover rate tables — get an itemised written quote before you book."
      ],
      [
        "What is the formula for packers and movers charges?",
        "Full Service Move Cost = (Packing + Loading + Transport + Unloading) + Insurance (3% of the declared goods value) + GST (18% on the full-service move) — servicesutra's published formula. This tool takes the packing, loading, transport and unloading range from its rate table (by home size and distance band), adds vehicle transport and stairs where they apply, adds 3% insurance on the declared value, then adds 18% GST on the subtotal."
      ],
      [
        "Do packers and movers charge GST — 5% or 18%?",
        "The guides disagree, and this page states both. servicesutra's formula charges 18% GST on a full-service move. InteriorCalculator notes that published guides describe 5% GST without input credit or 18% with it, and many treat a full packing and moving service as 18%. This tool uses 18% as the default. Ask the mover whether the quote includes GST and at what rate — a quote that excludes GST looks cheaper by exactly that amount."
      ],
      [
        "What is local vs intercity shifting?",
        "Local is under 50 km — within the same city — and intercity is 50 km and over (RentNiti's split). The distance band changes the range completely: a 2 BHK is ₹6,500–₹14,000 locally but ₹14,000–₹26,000 over 50–300 km and ₹18,000–₹35,000 over 300–1,000 km, before GST. Enter the road distance, not the straight-line distance."
      ],
      [
        "How much does it cost to transport a car or bike?",
        "By distance band. A car is ₹3,000–₹5,000 locally, ₹5,000–₹8,000 over 50–300 km, ₹7,000–₹10,000 over 300–1,000 km (DZ Cargo's 401–800 km car-component band exactly) and ₹8,000–₹10,000 over 1,000 km (servicesutra's Kolkata–Delhi small-car total exactly). A bike is ₹2,500–₹5,000 locally and ₹6,000–₹7,800 over 1,000 km (servicesutra's Kolkata–Delhi bike total exactly). DZ Cargo publishes no bike price at all — this tool does not invent one."
      ],
      [
        "What is transit insurance for packers and movers?",
        "Insurance on the declared value of the goods, charged at 3% of that value — servicesutra's formula, and the rate RentNiti and shiftingapp state. On ₹2,00,000 of goods that is ₹6,000; on ₹5,00,000 it is ₹15,000. InteriorCalculator states 2–3% — this tool uses the 3% formula rate. Enter 0 if you are not taking insurance; the tool then shows no insurance in the total."
      ],
      [
        "Do movers charge extra for stairs?",
        "Yes, where there is no lift. RentNiti states ₹150–₹400 per flight of stairs, and this tool uses that band: 2 flights add ₹300–₹800 to the move range. shiftingapp states a different basis — ₹200–₹500 per floor above the 2nd floor — and the page says so. Count the flights at both addresses."
      ],
      [
        "Why do different guides give different prices for the same move?",
        "Because they measure different things. servicesutra's Kolkata–Delhi table is a city-pair total; InteriorCalculator's is a distance-band table; DZ Cargo's is an operator's indicative table; shiftingapp's is a band across listed partners. For a 3 BHK over 1,000 km, servicesutra says ₹29,570–₹39,298 and InteriorCalculator says ₹42,000–₹75,000. This tool follows InteriorCalculator for the 1,000+ km band and prints the disagreement wherever it affects a figure — the range is the honest answer, not a single price."
      ],
      [
        "Is this the exact price I will pay?",
        "No — it is a planning range from published mover rate tables, not a quotation. The actual price depends on the volume of goods, the packing quality, the floor and lift access, the date (weekends and month-ends cost more) and the mover. Get a physical or video survey and an itemised written quote covering tolls, GST and insurance before you book, and photograph high-value items before packing."
      ],
      [
        "What is not included in this estimate?",
        "Unpacking and rearranging at the destination, dismantling and reassembly of furniture, AC uninstallation and installation, TV wall-mount dismantling, temporary storage, and any tolls the mover passes on — unless the mover's quote says otherwise. This tool covers packing, loading, transport, unloading, vehicle transport, stairs, transit insurance and GST only. DZ Cargo asks for an individual quote for journeys above 1,900 km; this tool's 1,000+ km band runs to 2,000 km and is a planning range."
      ]
    ],
