    "rateTitle": "Packers and movers charges in India — base range by home size and distance",
    "rulesNote": "Seven rules, each one checkable against the sources. Nothing here is a guess — and where a source states a figure differently, the page says so.",
    "rulesRows": [
      {
        "detail": "Local is under 50 km and intercity is 50 km and over (RentNiti's split). The band sets the base range: a 2 BHK is ₹6,500–₹14,000 locally, ₹14,000–₹26,000 over 50–300 km, ₹18,000–₹35,000 over 300–1,000 km and ₹28,000–₹34,000 over 1,000 km. Enter the road distance, not the straight-line distance.",
        "rule": "Local is under 50 km; intercity is 50 km and over"
      },
      {
        "detail": "Full Service Move Cost = (Packing + Loading + Transport + Unloading) + Insurance (3% of the declared goods value) + GST (18% on the full-service move) — servicesutra's published formula. The base range is the bracket: packing, loading, transport and unloading together.",
        "rule": "The formula is servicesutra's: (P+L+T+U) + insurance + GST"
      },
      {
        "detail": "The base range is split into packing + loading 27%, transport 57% and unloading 16% — servicesutra's Kolkata–Delhi component shares, averaged across its five home-size rows. The split is indicative: the published tables quote packing + loading + transport + unloading as one range, and servicesutra's city-pair table is the only published component split. The three components always sum exactly to the move range.",
        "rule": "The split is 27% packing + loading, 57% transport, 16% unloading"
      },
      {
        "detail": "Stairs are flights × ₹150–₹400 per flight (RentNiti). Shiftingapp states a different basis — ₹200–₹500 per floor above the 2nd floor. This tool uses RentNiti's per-flight band: 2 flights add ₹300–₹800 to the move range, at both addresses.",
        "rule": "Stairs are ₹150–₹400 per flight, at both addresses"
      },
      {
        "detail": "Car transport follows DZ Cargo's car-component bands (up to 400 km ₹3,000–₹5,000; 401–800 km ₹7,000–₹10,000) and servicesutra's Kolkata–Delhi small-car total (₹8,000–₹10,000). Bike transport follows servicesutra's Kolkata–Delhi bike total (₹6,000–₹7,800). DZ Cargo publishes no bike price at all. Bike + car is the sum of the two ranges.",
        "rule": "Vehicle transport is priced by distance band, from the published tables"
      },
      {
        "detail": "Insurance is 3% of the declared goods value (servicesutra, RentNiti, shiftingapp); InteriorCalculator states 2–3%. This tool uses the 3% formula rate: ₹6,000 on ₹2,00,000 of goods, ₹15,000 on ₹5,00,000. Enter 0 if you are not taking insurance.",
        "rule": "Transit insurance is 3% of the declared goods value"
      },
      {
        "detail": "GST is 18% of the subtotal (move + vehicle + insurance) — servicesutra's formula for a full-service move. InteriorCalculator notes published guides describe 5% GST without input credit or 18% with it. This tool uses 18% as the default and states the 5% alternative plainly: a quote that excludes GST looks cheaper by exactly that amount.",
        "rule": "GST is 18% on the full-service subtotal; 5% is the stated alternative"
      }
    ],
    "rulesTitle": "The rules behind the answer",
