// Laptop budget checker.
// Budget -> band -> the minimum spec to look for, by use case.
// The bands and the spec in each cell come from the published
// Indian laptop guides checked 12 November 2026 (see sources.md):
// TheGadgetGyaan (7 Nov 2026 prices), Fincash (8 Nov), benchmarksutra
// (6 Nov), 91mobiles (July), umatechnology, techbloat, reviews-4u,
// prodasc. The tool recommends a SPEC, not a model; the prices in the
// band table are a dated snapshot (checked 12 November 2026) and the
// page says so. The three facts that shape the table:
// - Memory chip prices nearly doubled in 2026 and Dell/HP/Lenovo
//   laptops rose 15-30% (Business Today via TheGadgetGyaan), so
//   Rs 50,000 buys less than it did in July: the ThinkBook 16 was
//   Rs 46,990 in July (91mobiles) and about Rs 74,000 in November.
// - A Core i5 / Ryzen 5 with 16GB starts at about Rs 60,000-65,000
//   (Acer Aspire 3 i5-1334U 16GB about Rs 61,390, TheGadgetGyaan).
// - 16GB is the 2026 floor for multitasking and 512GB SSD the
//   minimum for Windows (techbloat, prodasc); the cheapest 16GB
//   laptop in benchmarksutra's November sample is Rs 56,990.
// - Dedicated graphics for AAA gaming start with the RTX 4050 at
//   about Rs 75,000 (techbloat's Rs 75,000-1,50,000 gaming band);
//   the RTX 2050 tier starts near Rs 59,000 (Vivobook 16X).
// Bands are half-open on the top: a budget belongs to the first
// band whose max it does not exceed; Rs 1,20,000 and above is the
