// TDS calculator (India, FY 2026-27).
// TDS (tax deducted at source) is the tax the payer withholds before
// making a payment, at the rate and threshold of the payment's section
// under the Income-tax Act, 2025: salary in section 392, almost
// everything else in the tables of section 393, the no-PAN rule in
// section 397(2). The rates and thresholds are those of the CBDT TDS
// rate chart for tax year 2026-27, unchanged from FY 2025-26.
//   TDS = taxable base x section rate
// For most sections the taxable base is the WHOLE amount, once it
// crosses the threshold: a Rs.1,00,000 professional fee above the
// Rs.50,000 limit is taxed on the full Rs.1,00,000, not just the
// Rs.50,000 above the limit. Two sections are the exception, taxed
// only on the amount ABOVE the threshold: purchase of goods (194Q)
// and cash withdrawals (194N).
// Thresholds are tested per year, per month or per transaction,
// depending on the section; two use "at or above" (>=): property
// purchase (Rs.50 lakh or more) and premature EPF withdrawal
// (Rs.50,000 or more). Every other threshold uses "exceeds" (>).
// Salary has no fixed rate: the employer estimates the year's tax on
// the new-regime slabs - Rs.75,000 standard deduction, the section
// 87A rebate up to Rs.60,000 for taxable income up to Rs.12,00,000
// with marginal relief just above it, surcharge above Rs.50 lakh and
// 4% health and education cess - and deducts it in twelve equal
// monthly instalments. The slab, surcharge and rebate rules here
// mirror the site's own income tax calculator (entry 259) and salary
// calculator (entry 315), which carry the same FY 2026-27 figures.
// Without a PAN, section 397(2) requires the higher of the section
// rate, the rate in force and 20% - except purchase of goods and
// e-commerce payments, where the higher rate is 5%. Winnings stay
// at 30%, which is already higher than 20%.
// No surcharge or cess is added to TDS on payments to residents
// (salary is the exception, because its TDS is the full slab tax).
// Conventions (stated on the page):
// - Amounts are from Rs.1 to Rs.10,00,00,000; TDS rounds to the
//   nearest rupee (half up, as in JS Math.round).
// - For "year" types the amount is the total paid to the payee in
//   the financial year; for "month" types it is the monthly payment;
//   for "transaction" types a single payment; for salary the annual
//   salary; for online-game winnings the net winnings.
// - The contractor threshold is Rs.30,000 a bill OR Rs.1,00,000 a
//   year: the calculator tests the year's total, and the single-bill
//   rule is stated on the page because one amount field cannot test
//   both.
// - The 194DA amount is the income component of the payout, not the
//   whole payout; the 194IA amount is the consideration (the
//   stamp-duty value is used if higher); the 194N amount is the
//   year's total cash withdrawn (filer position, Rs.1 crore limit).
export const TDS_MIN_AMOUNT = 1;
export const TDS_MAX_AMOUNT = 100000000;
export const TDS_STANDARD_DEDUCTION = 75000;
export const TDS_REBATE_LIMIT = 1200000;
export const TDS_REBATE_MAX = 60000;
export const TDS_CESS_RATE = 0.04;
export const TDS_NO_PAN_RATE = 20;
export const TDS_NO_PAN_RATE_GOODS = 5;

