    <section class="calc-section" id="method">
      <div class="calc-wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">The calculation, explained</p>
          <h2>The step-up SIP formula</h2>
          <p>${e(p.modelNote)}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="formula-banner">
          <small>The step-up SIP future-value rule, monthly compounding</small>
          Monthly SIP in year y = S × (1 + s)^(y − 1) · each instalment earns from the start of its month
        </div>

        <div class="grid3">
          <div class="math-step">
            1. The SIP rises every year
            <strong>Year 1 ${fmtINR(p.sampleMonthly)} a month · Year ${p.sampleYears} ${fmtINR(sample.finalSip)} a month</strong>
            <span>${fmtINR(p.sampleMonthly)} × 1.10^${p.sampleYears - 1} = ${fmtINR(sample.finalSip)} a month in year ${p.sampleYears}. The step-up applies once a year, at the start of each new year, and is kept unrounded inside the calculation.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="math-step">
            2. Each instalment compounds from its month
            <strong>Monthly rate ${sampleMonthlyRate.toFixed(7)} · ${p.sampleYears * 12} instalments</strong>
            <span>${p.sampleRate}% a year ÷ 12 ÷ 100 = ${sampleMonthlyRate.toFixed(7)} a month. Each instalment is paid at the start of its month and earns that month's return until the end — the same convention as this site's SIP calculator.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="math-step">
            3. The goal, worked backwards
            <strong>${fmtINR(sampleGoal.monthly)} a month reaches ${fmtINR(p.goalTarget)}</strong>
            <span>Starting at ${fmtINR(sampleGoal.monthly)} a month, rising ${p.sampleStepUp}% a year, reaches ${fmtINR(suCompute(sampleGoal.monthly, p.sampleStepUp, p.sampleRate, p.sampleYears).value)} in ${p.sampleYears} years at ${p.sampleRate}% — just above the ${fmtINR(p.goalTarget)} target — on ${fmtINR(suCompute(sampleGoal.monthly, p.sampleStepUp, p.sampleRate, p.sampleYears).invested)} invested. The starting SIP is rounded up to the next rupee.</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="callout">
          <strong>${fmtINR(sampleGoal.monthly)} a month at ${p.sampleRate}% reaches ${fmtINR(p.goalTarget)} in ${fmtNum(p.sampleYears)} years with a ${p.sampleStepUp}% step-up.</strong>
          Work backwards from a goal instead of forwards from an amount: the calculator shows the starting SIP any target needs at your assumed return, step-up and tenure. Raising ₹10,000 a month by 10% every year makes ₹33,74,326 in 10 years at 12%, on ₹19,12,491 invested, against ₹23,23,391 without the step-up.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

