    <section class="calc-section" id="overview">
      <div class="calc-wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Understand the result</p>
          <h2>${e(p.overviewTitle)}</h2>
          <p>${e(p.overview)}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid3">
          <article class="card">
            <span class="number-label">01 / THE MORATORIUM IS NOT FREE</span>
            <h3>Interest builds up while you study</h3>
            <p>On a ₹20 lakh loan at 9.5%, a 12-month moratorium adds ₹1,90,000 of simple interest. On a ₹50 lakh loan at 11% with a 24-month moratorium it adds ₹11,00,000. The holiday from EMIs is real — the interest is real too.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="number-label">02 / PAYING NOW BEATS PAYING LATER</span>
            <h3>₹15,833 a month saves ₹70,850</h3>
            <p>Pay the simple interest during the moratorium and the principal never grows: the EMI on the headline loan is ₹32,688 instead of ₹35,793, and the all-in cost is ₹70,850 lower. The saving is bigger on longer moratoriums — ₹7,18,300 on the ₹50 lakh example.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="number-label">03 / THE RATE SETS THE COST</span>
            <h3>1.5 points saves ₹1,86,353</h3>
            <p>On ₹20 lakh over 7 years with a 12-month moratorium, 9.5% costs ₹10,06,639 of interest in all; 11% costs ₹11,92,992. A lower rate saves money every month and over the whole loan — compare lenders on the rate before you sign.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

