    <section class="calc-section" id="method">
      <div class="calc-wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">The calculation, explained</p>
          <h2>How an education loan EMI is worked out</h2>
          <p>${e(p.modelNote)}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="formula-banner">
          <small>The education loan EMI rule</small>
          EMI = P × r × (1 + r)^n ÷ ((1 + r)^n − 1) · Moratorium interest = P × rate × months ÷ 12 ÷ 100
        </div>

        <div class="grid3">
          <div class="math-step">
            1. The moratorium interest
            <strong>₹20,00,000 × 9.5% × 12 ÷ 12 = ₹1,90,000</strong>
            <span>Simple interest on the loan amount for the 12 months of the moratorium — about ₹15,833 a month. It is the same whether you pay it now or let it add to the loan; what changes is what happens to it next.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="math-step">
            2. The EMI
            <strong>₹21,90,000 × ${rateDec(p.sampleRate)} × (1 + ${rateDec(p.sampleRate)})^84 ÷ ((1 + ${rateDec(p.sampleRate)})^84 − 1) = ₹35,793</strong>
            <span>The principal at EMI start is ₹21,90,000 — the loan plus the capitalised moratorium interest — at a monthly rate of 9.5% ÷ 12, over 84 monthly instalments. Pay the interest during the moratorium and the principal stays ₹20,00,000, giving an EMI of ₹32,688.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="math-step">
            3. The totals, and the comparison
            <strong>₹35,793 × 84 = ₹30,06,639 · Interest ₹10,06,639 · Pay now ₹32,688 → ₹29,35,789</strong>
            <span>The total repayment comes from the unrounded EMI, so the rounded EMI times 84 can differ from the total by a few rupees. The all-in interest is the repayment interest (₹8,16,639) plus the moratorium interest (₹1,90,000) — ₹10,06,639. Paying during the moratorium saves ₹70,850.</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="callout">
          <strong>₹35,793 a month on ₹20,00,000 at 9.5% over 7 years, after a 12-month moratorium.</strong>
          The moratorium adds ₹1,90,000 before repayment even starts. Paying about ₹15,833 a month while you study keeps the principal at ₹20,00,000, cuts the EMI to ₹32,688 and saves ₹70,850 over the loan.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

