    <section class="calc-section" id="overview">
      <div class="calc-wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Understand the result</p>
          <h2>${e(p.overviewTitle)}</h2>
          <p>${e(p.overview)}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid3">
          <article class="card">
            <span class="number-label">01 / TIMING IS THE WHOLE POINT</span>
            <h3>10.16% a year, not 35.29%</h3>
            <p>The absolute return ignores timing. XIRR weighs every rupee by how long it was invested, so it is the figure that compares with an FD rate or a fund benchmark — the 35.29% cannot be compared with anything annual.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="number-label">02 / JUDGED AGAINST THE SAFE ALTERNATIVE</span>
            <h3>₹20,452 ahead of an FD at 7%</h3>
            <p>Every flow grown at 7% to the valuation date would be worth ₹1,89,548. The comparison is built in, so a return can be judged against the safe alternative, not in isolation — and the ₹20,000 withdrawal counts against the FD figure too.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="number-label">03 / THE SAME ANSWER AS EXCEL</span>
            <h3>37.34% on Microsoft's example</h3>
            <p>Microsoft's own XIRR example — ₹10,000 in, ₹13,000 back over 15 months — gives 37.34% here and in Excel. Copy the flows into a sheet and =XIRR(values, dates) returns the same rate.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p>XIRR suits any investment with more than one dated flow — SIPs, top-ups, partial withdrawals, a portfolio built over years. It does not suit a single lumpsum, where the <a href="/cagr-calculator/">CAGR calculator</a> gives the same answer more directly. For the future value of a regular SIP, use the <a href="/sip-calculator/">SIP calculator</a>; for a one-off investment, the <a href="/lumpsum-calculator/">lumpsum calculator</a>; and for drawing an income from the holding, the <a href="/swp-calculator/">SWP calculator</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

