    <section class="calc-section soft" id="methodology">
      <div class="calc-wrap">
        <div class="method-box">
          <h2>About the method</h2>
          <p>
            Days between two dates = end day number minus start day
            number, computed in UTC as whole days, so time zones and
            daylight saving can never move a result. The start date is
            not counted and the end date is; counting both ends is the
            total plus one. Weeks = total days divided by 7, with the
            remainder shown. The years/months/days breakdown counts real
            calendar months by stepping forward from the start date,
            never by dividing by 30. Business days count Monday to
            Friday from the day after the start date through the end
            date; weekend days are the rest. Add or subtract moves by
            calendar days from the start date, weekends included, and
            the result is shown with its weekday. A countdown is the
            target date minus today, in whole days; today is not
            counted. Accepted dates run from 1 January 1900 to
            31 December 2100, and the largest offset is 36,500 days.
          </p>
          <p>
            The figures were checked 13 November 2026 against Calvix,
            The Tools Kit, CalculatorKing, iUnitConverter and
            datescalculator.org. Calvix reproduces exactly: 15 January
            to 25 December 2026 is 344 days, 11 months and 10 days,
            246 working days, 8,256 hours, and 345 days counting both
            ends; 24 September 2026 to 2 May 2027 is 220 days; 1
            February to 1 March is 29 days in 2028 and 28 days in
            2027; and a 90-day notice from 24 September 2026 counting
            both ends finishes on 22 December. The Tools Kit
            reproduces exactly: 1 October to 25 December 2026 is 85
            days, 12 weeks and 1 day; 30 days from 1 October 2026 is
            Saturday 31 October 2026; 90 days from 1 October 2026 is
            Wednesday 30 December 2026; 45 days before 1 October 2026
            is Monday 17 August 2026; and 1 January 2026 to 1 January
            2027 is 365 days. CalculatorKing reproduces exactly: the
            Indian financial year, 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027, is
            364 days, 52 weeks exactly. iUnitConverter reproduces
            exactly: 1 November to 7 November 2026 is 6 days, and 15
            August 1947 to 15 August 2026 is 28,855 days, 79 years.
            datescalculator.org reproduces exactly: 12 November to 26
            November 2026 is 14 days, with 10 weekdays and 4 weekend
            days. One convention difference is stated honestly: The
            Tools Kit counts business days from the start date itself,
            so its figure is one higher whenever the start date is a
            weekday — 62 instead of 61 for 1 October to 25 December
            2026, and 261 instead of 260 weekdays for the whole of
            2026. Neither figure is wrong; this page counts from the
            day after the start date, matching its total-days figure.
            Business days exclude Saturdays and Sundays only: Indian
            public holidays are not removed, because they vary by
            state and employer. This page counts calendar days, not
            legal deadlines. For related tools, the <a href="/age-calculator/">age
            calculator</a>, the <a href="/pregnancy-due-date-calculator/">pregnancy
            due date calculator</a>, the <a href="/ovulation-calculator/">ovulation
            calculator</a> and the <a href="/percentage-calculator/">percentage
            calculator</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Last updated 13 November 2026.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

