    <section class="calc-section" id="method">
      <div class="calc-wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">The formula</p>
          <h2>How fuel cost is worked out</h2>
          <p>${e(p.modelNote)}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="formula-banner">
          <small>The fuel cost formulas</small>
          Fuel needed = distance ÷ mileage · Trip cost = fuel needed × price · Cost per km = price ÷ mileage · Cost per person = trip cost ÷ passengers · Monthly cost = (km per day × days per month ÷ mileage) × price
        </div>

        <div class="grid3">
          <div class="math-step">
            1. The fuel
            <strong>280 ÷ 15 = 18.67 litres</strong>
            <span>Distance divided by mileage. For CNG the same division gives kg, because CNG mileage is km per kg.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="math-step">
            2. The cost
            <strong>(280 ÷ 15) × ₹95.00 = ₹1,773.33</strong>
            <span>Fuel times price. The cost per km is ₹95.00 ÷ 15 = ₹6.33 — the distance cancels out.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="math-step">
            3. The check
            <strong>Seventeen published examples reproduce exactly</strong>
            <span>codingmarble: ₹1,773 and ₹3,547. freefuelbill: ₹3,500 and ₹2,375. dailytools: ₹1,110, ₹2,220 and ₹555 each. calcwise: ₹3,467.</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="callout">
          <strong>₹1,773.33 — the fuel cost of Delhi to Jaipur.</strong>
          18.67 litres at ₹95.00 a litre, one way; ₹3,546.67 for the return leg.
        </div>

        <p>Three honest limits, and the page states them: the price is entered by you — the November 2026 Delhi defaults (petrol ₹102.12, diesel ₹95.20, CNG ₹86.98 a kg) are checked, not live, and prices change by city and by day. Mileage is your vehicle's real-world figure, not the brochure figure — the gap can be worth ₹500 on one Delhi–Jaipur leg. And tolls, parking and FASTag are not in the figure: this tool counts fuel only.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

