    <section class="calc-section" id="methodology">
      <div class="calc-wrap">
        <div class="method-box">
          <h2>About the method</h2>
          <p>
            Average price = total invested ÷ total shares, where total invested is the sum over the lots of price × quantity. Current value = total shares × current market price. Profit or loss = current value − total invested, in rupees and as a percentage of the total invested. The rise to the average = (average price − current price) ÷ current price, from the average as shown. Shares to buy for a target average = current quantity × (current average − target) ÷ (target − new price), rounded UP to a whole share — and only when the target lies strictly between the current average and the new price. Money is rounded to paise; shares are whole numbers. Brokerage, STT, stamp duty and other charges are NOT included.
          </p>
          <p>
            The figures were checked 14 November 2026 against stocknotify, rupeescalc, blogbanking, thebeststockbroker and a2z. stocknotify reproduces exactly: 40 shares at ₹250 and 30 at ₹220 average ₹237.14 on ₹16,600 for 70 shares; 100 at ₹500, 50 at ₹440 and 50 at ₹410 average ₹462.50; and its planner gives 67 shares for a ₹460 target at ₹400, costing ₹26,800 for a new average of ₹459.88. rupeescalc reproduces exactly before charges: 100 at ₹200, 50 at ₹160 and 75 at ₹130 average ₹167.78 on ₹37,750 for 225 shares — its ₹168.24 is the charges-inclusive average, adding its ₹105 of charges, and this tool takes no charges. blogbanking reproduces exactly: 50 at ₹1,480, 30 at ₹1,320 and 20 at ₹1,210 average ₹1,378 on ₹1,37,800 for 100 shares, and its planner table gives 19, 37, 78 and 256 shares for targets of ₹1,350, ₹1,330, ₹1,300 and ₹1,250. thebeststockbroker reproduces exactly: 100 at ₹200 and 50 at ₹160 average ₹186.67 on ₹28,000 for 150 shares. a2z reproduces exactly: 100 at ₹250 and 50 at ₹200 average ₹233.33, not ₹225, and its planner gives 200 shares, costing ₹42,000, for a ₹220 target at ₹210. For related tools, the <a href="/xirr-calculator/">XIRR calculator</a>, the <a href="/cagr-calculator/">CAGR calculator</a>, the <a href="/lumpsum-calculator/">Lumpsum calculator</a> and the <a href="/capital-gains-tax-calculator/">Capital Gains Tax calculator</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Last updated 14 November 2026.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

