// Brokerage calculator (India), NSE / BSE equity and MCX, rates as of
// November 2026. Every charge on an Indian contract note, worked out
// in the browser: brokerage, STT / CTT, exchange transaction charges,
// the SEBI turnover fee, stamp duty, the DP charge on delivery sells
// and 18% GST — then gross P&L, net P&L and the break-even price.
// - Rates (verified 14 November 2026 against Zerodha's own charges
//   page, Groww's pricing page, Upstox's pricing page and Angel One's
//   pricing pages, plus the NSE / BSE tariff schedules they reproduce):
//   NSE transaction charges from 1 March 2026 — equity 0.00307%,
//   futures 0.00183%, options 0.03553% of premium (IPFT included);
//   BSE — equity 0.00375%, futures 0, options 0.0325% of premium.
//   STT from 1 April 2026 (Finance Act 2026) — delivery 0.1% on buy
//   and sell, intraday 0.025% on sell, futures 0.05% on sell, options
//   0.15% of the premium sold. Stamp duty on the buy side — delivery
//   0.015%, intraday 0.003%, futures 0.002%, options 0.003%. SEBI
//   turnover fee Rs 10 per crore (0.0001% of turnover). GST 18% on
//   brokerage + exchange transaction charges + SEBI fee — not on STT,
//   stamp duty or the DP charge. MCX (non-agricultural only): CTT
//   0.01% on futures sells and 0.05% on options premium sold; MCX
//   transaction charge 0.0021% (futures) and 0.0418% of premium
//   (options); stamp 0.002% / 0.003% on the buy side.
// - The 2026 revisions are why older calculators disagree: the
//   pre-March NSE equity charge was 0.00297% (now 0.00307%), and the
//   pre-April STT on futures was 0.02% and on options 0.10% (now
//   0.05% and 0.15%). The "0.03%" figure sometimes quoted as intraday
//   STT is brokerage, not STT — Zerodha's intraday brokerage is
//   0.03% capped at Rs 20; intraday STT is 0.025% on the sell side.
//   The "0.02%" stamp duty figure is wrong: delivery stamp duty is
//   0.015% and intraday 0.003% on the buy side.
// - Broker presets (each broker's own published charges page):
//   Zerodha — delivery Rs 0, intraday / futures the lower of Rs 20
//   or 0.03% per executed order, options flat Rs 20. Groww — delivery
//   / intraday the lower of Rs 20 or 0.1%, minimum Rs 5, F&O flat
//   Rs 20. Upstox — delivery Rs 20 flat, intraday the lower of Rs 20
//   or 0.1%, futures the lower of Rs 20 or 0.05%, options Rs 20.
//   Angel One — delivery / intraday the lower of Rs 20 or 0.1%,
//   minimum Rs 5, F&O flat Rs 20. Flat Rs 20 — a generic discount
//   broker at Rs 20 per executed order in every segment.
// - DP charge on delivery sells, per scrip (including GST): Zerodha
//   Rs 15.34 (Rs 3.5 CDSL + Rs 9.5 Zerodha + Rs 2.34 GST — Zerodha's
//   own charges page; the "Rs 13.5 + GST = Rs 15.93" figure quoted
//   by third-party sites conflicts with Zerodha's own page and is
//   not used); Groww, Upstox, Angel One and flat Rs 20: Rs 20 + GST
//   = Rs 23.60. The DP charge is a flat per-scrip amount, not per
//   share, and it applies only when shares leave demat — delivery
//   sells only, never intraday or F&O.
// - Rounding: every charge is computed unrounded; each displayed
//   line is rounded to paise (half up); the TOTAL is the unrounded
//   sum rounded to paise — so the displayed lines can differ from
//   the total by a paisa. Net P&L = gross P&L - total charges.
//   Break-even is the sell price at which net P&L is exactly zero,
//   found by bisection on the sell price (charges that scale with
//   the exit price are re-computed at each trial price). The
//   break-even price is rounded to paise, so the net P&L at the
//   rounded break-even can be up to half a paisa per share from
//   zero — the Python model allows the same.
// - What this tool does NOT model, and says so on the page:
//   call-and-trade and auto-square-off fees (Rs 50-75 per order),
//   account maintenance charges, pledge fees, payment-gateway fees,
//   interest on margin funding, option exercise / assignment, BSE
//   scrip-group variation (the calculator uses the standard group
//   A/B rate of 0.00375%), currency trades, and income tax on the
//   profit (see the Capital Gains Tax calculator). One buy order and
//   one sell order are assumed; split fills can attract brokerage
//   on each part. The contract note is the final record.
// - Anchors, checked 14 November 2026 against the independent
//   Python model: tradeprofy delivery (100 @ Rs 500 -> Rs 520,
//   Zerodha) — total Rs 128.66, net Rs 1,871.34; tradeprofy intraday
//   (100 @ Rs 1,000 -> Rs 1,010, Zerodha) — total Rs 82.97, net
//   Rs 917.03, break-even Rs 1,000.83; tradeprofy futures (1 Nifty
//   lot, 65 @ 25,000 -> 25,100) — STT Rs 815.75, total Rs 969.61,
//   net Rs 5,530.39; tradeprofy options (1 Nifty lot, 65, premium
//   Rs 150 -> Rs 180) — total Rs 74.06, net Rs 1,875.94; finaura
//   intraday (100 @ Rs 1,000 -> Rs 1,020, Zerodha) — total Rs 83.26,
//   net Rs 1,916.74, break-even Rs 1,000.83; Groww delivery (same
//   trade as tradeprofy's delivery example) — total Rs 184.12, net
//   Rs 1,815.88 ("about Rs 184"); papertradingapp delivery (50 @
//   Rs 1,000 -> Rs 1,100, Zerodha) — total Rs 131.77, net
//   Rs 4,868.23, against their approximate "~Rs 132 / ~Rs 4,868".
// - This is an estimate for planning only, not investment advice.
//   Nothing is sent anywhere: every calculation runs in the browser.
// Conventions (stated on the page):
// - The client sends exactly the 7 BR_KEYS.
// - Segment is "delivery", "intraday", "futures", "options",
//   "mcx-futures" or "mcx-options". Exchange is "nse" or "bse"
//   (MCX segments use MCX rates whatever the exchange says).
//   Broker is "zerodha", "groww", "upstox", "angelone" or "flat20".
// - Buy price is a finite number over Rs 0 up to Rs 10,00,000; sell
//   price is a finite number from Rs 0 up to Rs 10,00,000; quantity
//   is a whole number from 1 to 10,00,000 (shares, or units — for
//   F&O, the lot size times the number of lots). includeDp is a
//   boolean and applies only to delivery sells.
export const BR_MAX_PRICE = 1000000;
export const BR_MAX_QTY = 1000000;
export const BR_KEYS = ["segment", "exchange", "broker", "buyPrice", "sellPrice", "quantity", "includeDp"];
export const BR_SEGMENTS = ["delivery", "intraday", "futures", "options", "mcx-futures", "mcx-options"];
export const BR_EXCHANGES = ["nse", "bse"];
export const BR_BROKERS = ["zerodha", "groww", "upstox", "angelone", "flat20"];
export const BR_SEGMENT_RATES = {
  delivery: { sttBuy: 0.001, sttSell: 0.001, stamp: 0.00015, exchNse: 0.0000307, exchBse: 0.0000375 },
  intraday: { sttBuy: 0, sttSell: 0.00025, stamp: 0.00003, exchNse: 0.0000307, exchBse: 0.0000375 },
  futures: { sttBuy: 0, sttSell: 0.0005, stamp: 0.00002, exchNse: 0.0000183, exchBse: 0 },
  options: { sttBuy: 0, sttSell: 0.0015, stamp: 0.00003, exchNse: 0.0003553, exchBse: 0.000325 },
  "mcx-futures": { sttBuy: 0, sttSell: 0.0001, stamp: 0.00002, exchNse: 0.000021, exchBse: 0.000021 },
  "mcx-options": { sttBuy: 0, sttSell: 0.0005, stamp: 0.00003, exchNse: 0.000418, exchBse: 0.000418 }
};
export const BR_SEBI_RATE = 0.000001;
export const BR_GST_RATE = 0.18;
export const BR_DP = { zerodha: 15.34, groww: 23.6, upstox: 23.6, angelone: 23.6, flat20: 23.6 };

export function brRound2(x) {
  return Math.round(x * 100) / 100;
}

export function brBrokerageLeg(broker, segment, value) {
  if (value <= 0) return 0;
  if (broker === "zerodha") {
    if (segment === "delivery") return 0;
    if (segment === "options" || segment === "mcx-options") return 20;
    return Math.min(20, 0.0003 * value);
  }
  if (broker === "groww") {
    if (segment === "delivery" || segment === "intraday") return Math.max(5, Math.min(20, 0.001 * value));
    return 20;
  }
  if (broker === "upstox") {
    if (segment === "delivery") return 20;
    if (segment === "intraday") return Math.min(20, 0.001 * value);
    if (segment === "futures") return Math.min(20, 0.0005 * value);
    return 20;
  }
  if (broker === "angelone") {
    if (segment === "delivery" || segment === "intraday") return Math.max(5, Math.min(20, 0.001 * value));
    return 20;
  }
  return 20;
}

export function brCharges(input, sellPrice) {
  const rates = BR_SEGMENT_RATES[input.segment];
  const buy = input.buyPrice;
  const sell = sellPrice === undefined ? input.sellPrice : sellPrice;
  const qty = input.quantity;
  const buyValue = buy * qty;
  const sellValue = sell * qty;
  const exchRate = input.segment.indexOf("mcx-") === 0 ? rates.exchNse : (input.exchange === "nse" ? rates.exchNse : rates.exchBse);
  const brokerage = brBrokerageLeg(input.broker, input.segment, buyValue) + brBrokerageLeg(input.broker, input.segment, sellValue);
  const stt = rates.sttBuy * buyValue + rates.sttSell * sellValue;
  const exchange = exchRate * (buyValue + sellValue);
  const sebi = BR_SEBI_RATE * (buyValue + sellValue);
  const stamp = rates.stamp * buyValue;
  const dp = (input.segment === "delivery" && input.includeDp) ? BR_DP[input.broker] : 0;
  const gst = BR_GST_RATE * (brokerage + exchange + sebi);
  return {
    buyValue, sellValue, turnover: buyValue + sellValue,
    brokerage, stt, exchange, sebi, stamp, dp, gst,
    total: brokerage + stt + exchange + sebi + stamp + dp + gst
  };
}

export function brBreakEven(input) {
  const buy = input.buyPrice;
  const qty = input.quantity;
  if (buy <= 0 || qty <= 0) return null;
  const netAt = sell => (sell - buy) * qty - brCharges(input, sell).total;
  let lo = 0;
  let hi = buy + Math.max(1, brCharges(input).total / qty * 2 + 10);
  if (netAt(lo) >= 0) return 0;
  while (netAt(hi) < 0) {
    hi = buy + (hi - buy) * 2 + 10;
    if (hi > 1e9) return null;
  }
  for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
    const mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
    if (netAt(mid) < 0) lo = mid;
    else hi = mid;
  }
  return (lo + hi) / 2;
}

export function brCompute(input) {
  if (!input || typeof input !== "object" || Array.isArray(input)) return null;
  const keys = Object.keys(input);
  if (keys.length !== BR_KEYS.length) return null;
  for (const k of BR_KEYS) {
    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(input, k)) return null;
  }
  const segment = input.segment;
  const exchange = input.exchange;
  const broker = input.broker;
  const buyPrice = input.buyPrice;
  const sellPrice = input.sellPrice;
  const quantity = input.quantity;
  const includeDp = input.includeDp;
  if (BR_SEGMENTS.indexOf(segment) === -1) return null;
  if (BR_EXCHANGES.indexOf(exchange) === -1) return null;
  if (BR_BROKERS.indexOf(broker) === -1) return null;
  if (typeof buyPrice !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(buyPrice) || buyPrice <= 0 || buyPrice > BR_MAX_PRICE) return null;
  if (typeof sellPrice !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(sellPrice) || sellPrice < 0 || sellPrice > BR_MAX_PRICE) return null;
  if (typeof quantity !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(quantity) || !Number.isInteger(quantity) || quantity < 1 || quantity > BR_MAX_QTY) return null;
  if (typeof includeDp !== "boolean") return null;
  const c = brCharges(input);
  const gross = (sellPrice - buyPrice) * quantity;
  const total = brRound2(c.total);
  const net = brRound2(gross - total);
  const be = brBreakEven(input);
  return {
    segment, exchange, broker,
    buyValue: brRound2(c.buyValue), sellValue: brRound2(c.sellValue),
    turnover: brRound2(c.turnover),
    brokerage: brRound2(c.brokerage), stt: brRound2(c.stt),
    exchangeCharge: brRound2(c.exchange), sebi: brRound2(c.sebi),
    stamp: brRound2(c.stamp), dp: brRound2(c.dp), gst: brRound2(c.gst),
    totalCharges: total,
    grossPL: brRound2(gross), netPL: net,
    chargesPct: c.turnover > 0 ? brRound2(total / c.turnover * 100) : 0,
    breakEven: be === null ? null : brRound2(be),
    breakEvenMove: be === null ? null : brRound2(be - buyPrice),
    breakEvenPct: be === null || buyPrice <= 0 ? null : brRound2((be - buyPrice) / buyPrice * 100)
  };
}

