// Rooftop solar calculator (India), PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana.
// The subsidy, system size, generation, bill savings, payback and
// 25-year savings for a home rooftop solar system, worked out in the
// browser.
// - Rules (verified 14 November 2026 — see sources.md): PM Surya
//   Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana, approved by the Union Cabinet on
//   29 February 2024 (PIB Release ID 2010130, reproduced verbatim on
//   pmindia.gov.in): Central Financial Assistance of 60% of system
//   cost for 2 kW systems and 40% of the additional cost for systems
//   between 2 and 3 kW, capped at 3 kW — at current benchmark prices
//   Rs 30,000 for 1 kW, Rs 60,000 for 2 kW and Rs 78,000 for 3 kW or
//   more. A 3 kW system generates more than 300 units a month on
//   average. Outlay Rs 75,021 crore; one crore households; free
//   electricity up to 300 units a month; collateral-free loans of
//   around 7% for systems up to 3 kW.
// - MNRE operational guidelines for the CFA component (reported by
//   SolarQuarter, 1 September 2026, from the guidelines): the
//   standard subsidy is Rs 30,000 per kW for the first 2 kW and
//   Rs 18,000 for the third kW, maximum Rs 78,000. Special-category
//   states and UTs — the North-Eastern states, Uttarakhand, Himachal
//   Pradesh, Jammu & Kashmir, Ladakh, Andaman & Nicobar Islands and
//   Lakshadweep — get Rs 33,000 per kW for the first 2 kW and
//   Rs 19,800 for the third kW (cap Rs 85,800). Group housing
//   societies and resident welfare associations get Rs 18,000 per kW
//   (Rs 19,800 in special-category states) for common facilities,
//   up to 500 kW. Residential subsidy only under the capex model;
//   panels must meet the Domestic Content Requirement.
// - The national portal (pmsuryaghar.gov.in) could not be fetched
//   from this environment (HTTP 403 on 14 November 2026 — not
//   retried); the scheme rules above rest on the Cabinet release
//   and the MNRE-guidelines reproduction, stated honestly in
//   sources.md. The portal address itself is the one the Cabinet
//   release names.
// - Generation: 1 kW makes about 4 units a day, 1,460 units a year
//   (palz; risprilabs' range is 1,300-1,500 units a year per kW).
//   Suggested size = yearly units / 1,460, rounded up to the next
//   0.25 kW, capped at 10 kW (the residential scheme limit).
// - Roof: about 10 m2 of shadow-free roof per kW (risprilabs).
// - CO2: CEA CO2 Baseline Database for the Indian Power Sector,
//   Version 21.0 (November 2025): the weighted average emission
//   factor of the Indian Grid for FY 2024-25 is 0.710 tCO2/MWh
//   (adjusted for cross-border electricity transfers).
// - Savings: units the system makes replace units bought at the
//   tariff; surplus units are paid at the DISCOM's surplus rate.
//   Payback = net cost / yearly savings (null when yearly savings
//   are zero). 25-year savings = 25 x yearly savings - net cost,
//   with no allowance for panel degradation (about 0.5% a year,
//   per risprilabs) or future tariff rises — both would move the
//   figure, in opposite directions, and the page says so.
// - The tariff (default Rs 7.00 a unit) and the surplus rate
//   (default Rs 3.00 a unit) are editable assumptions, dated
//   November 2026 — never a state tariff stated as fact. The cost
//   per kW (default Rs 60,000) is an editable November 2026
//   benchmark from vendor quotes and the published price guides
//   (Rs 55,000-85,000 per kW); get a written quote before buying.
//   The net-meter cost (default Rs 0) is a separate one-off charge
//   your vendor may bill apart from the per-kW price.
// - Anchors, checked 14 November 2026 against the independent
//   Python model: palz — 300 units a month, 3 kW at Rs 60,000 a kW
//   = Rs 1,80,000, subsidy Rs 78,000, net Rs 1,02,000, 4,380 units
//   a year (365 a month), 3,600 replaced at Rs 7 and 780 surplus at
//   Rs 3, saving Rs 27,540 a year, payback 3.7 years; solarsense —
//   1 kW at Rs 67,184 a kW (Mono PERC-adjusted benchmark) + Rs 8,000
//   net meter = Rs 75,184, subsidy Rs 30,000, net Rs 45,184; 2 kW
//   = Rs 1,42,368, subsidy Rs 60,000, net Rs 82,368; Cabinet
//   release — a 3 kW system makes more than 300 units a month
//   (this model: 365); special-category 3 kW — subsidy Rs 85,800,
//   net Rs 94,200 on a Rs 1,80,000 system.
// - risprilabs is a consistency check, not an exact reproduction:
//   they size from peak sun hours x performance ratio
//   (5 x 365 x 75% = 1,368.75 units a year per kW) and round up to
//   whole 550 Wp panels — 2.75 kW making 3,764 units a year for a
//   300-unit home. This calculator uses 4 units a day per kW
//   (1,460 a year), so the same home gets a suggested 2.5 kW and
//   3,650 units a year. Both sit inside risprilabs' own 1,300-1,500
//   range, and palz agrees the suggested size is "about 2.5 kW".
// - Rounding: every amount is computed unrounded; each displayed
//   figure is rounded to paise (half up). Payback is rounded to
//   2 decimals; CO2 to 2 decimals in tonnes.
// - This is an estimate for planning only, not a quote or
//   engineering advice. Nothing is sent anywhere: every
//   calculation runs in the browser.
// Conventions (stated on the page):
// - The client sends exactly the 8 SO_KEYS.
// - stateCategory is "normal" or "special". roofAreaM2 is null
//   (not entered) or a finite number from 0 up to 10,000.
// - monthlyUnits is a finite number from 0 up to 5,000.
//   systemSizeKw is a finite number from 0.25 up to 10, in steps
//   of 0.25. tariff is a finite number from 0 up to 50.
//   surplusRate is a finite number from 0 up to 20. costPerKw is
//   a finite number from Rs 1,000 up to Rs 2,00,000. netMeterCost
//   is a finite number from Rs 0 up to Rs 50,000.
export const SO_GEN_PER_KW_YEAR = 1460;
export const SO_ROOF_M2_PER_KW = 10;
export const SO_CO2_T_PER_MWH = 0.71;
export const SO_MAX_SIZE_KW = 10;
export const SO_SIZE_STEP = 0.25;
export const SO_MAX_UNITS = 5000;
export const SO_MAX_TARIFF = 50;
export const SO_MAX_SURPLUS_RATE = 20;
export const SO_MAX_ROOF_M2 = 10000;
export const SO_MIN_COST_PER_KW = 1000;
export const SO_MAX_COST_PER_KW = 200000;
export const SO_MAX_NET_METER_COST = 50000;
export const SO_SUBSIDY_NORMAL = [30000, 18000, 78000];
export const SO_SUBSIDY_SPECIAL = [33000, 19800, 85800];
export const SO_KEYS = ["monthlyUnits", "systemSizeKw", "tariff", "surplusRate", "roofAreaM2", "stateCategory", "costPerKw", "netMeterCost"];
export const SO_STATE_CATEGORIES = ["normal", "special"];
export function soRound2(x) {
  return Math.floor(x * 100 + 0.5) / 100;
}
export function soSuggestedSize(monthlyUnits) {
  if (monthlyUnits <= 0) return 0;
  const raw = monthlyUnits * 12 / SO_GEN_PER_KW_YEAR;
  return Math.min(SO_MAX_SIZE_KW, Math.ceil(raw * 4 - 1e-9) / 4);
}
export function soSubsidyFor(size, category) {
  const rates = category === "special" ? SO_SUBSIDY_SPECIAL : SO_SUBSIDY_NORMAL;
  return Math.min(size, 2) * rates[0] + Math.max(0, Math.min(size - 2, 1)) * rates[1];
}
export function soCompute(input) {
  if (!input || typeof input !== "object") return null;
  const monthlyUnits = input.monthlyUnits;
  const systemSizeKw = input.systemSizeKw;
  const tariff = input.tariff;
  const surplusRate = input.surplusRate;
  const roofAreaM2 = input.roofAreaM2;
  const stateCategory = input.stateCategory;
  const costPerKw = input.costPerKw;
  const netMeterCost = input.netMeterCost;
  if (typeof monthlyUnits !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(monthlyUnits) || monthlyUnits < 0 || monthlyUnits > SO_MAX_UNITS) return null;
  if (typeof systemSizeKw !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(systemSizeKw) || systemSizeKw < SO_SIZE_STEP || systemSizeKw > SO_MAX_SIZE_KW || Math.abs(systemSizeKw * 4 - Math.round(systemSizeKw * 4)) > 1e-9) return null;
  if (typeof tariff !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(tariff) || tariff < 0 || tariff > SO_MAX_TARIFF) return null;
  if (typeof surplusRate !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(surplusRate) || surplusRate < 0 || surplusRate > SO_MAX_SURPLUS_RATE) return null;
  if (roofAreaM2 !== null && (typeof roofAreaM2 !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(roofAreaM2) || roofAreaM2 < 0 || roofAreaM2 > SO_MAX_ROOF_M2)) return null;
  if (SO_STATE_CATEGORIES.indexOf(stateCategory) === -1) return null;
  if (typeof costPerKw !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(costPerKw) || costPerKw < SO_MIN_COST_PER_KW || costPerKw > SO_MAX_COST_PER_KW) return null;
  if (typeof netMeterCost !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(netMeterCost) || netMeterCost < 0 || netMeterCost > SO_MAX_NET_METER_COST) return null;
  const annualUnits = soRound2(monthlyUnits * 12);
  const annualGenerationUnits = systemSizeKw * SO_GEN_PER_KW_YEAR;
  const monthlyGenerationUnits = soRound2(annualGenerationUnits / 12);
  const systemCost = soRound2(systemSizeKw * costPerKw + netMeterCost);
  const subsidy = soRound2(soSubsidyFor(systemSizeKw, stateCategory));
  const netCost = soRound2(systemCost - subsidy);
  const replacedUnits = Math.min(annualGenerationUnits, annualUnits);
  const surplusUnits = soRound2(annualGenerationUnits - replacedUnits);
  const annualSavings = soRound2(replacedUnits * tariff + surplusUnits * surplusRate);
  const monthlySavings = soRound2(annualSavings / 12);
  const paybackYears = annualSavings > 0 ? soRound2(netCost / annualSavings) : null;
  const savings25y = soRound2(25 * annualSavings - netCost);
  const co2PerYearT = soRound2(annualGenerationUnits / 1000 * SO_CO2_T_PER_MWH);
  const co2_25yT = soRound2(annualGenerationUnits / 1000 * SO_CO2_T_PER_MWH * 25);
  const roofAreaRequiredM2 = soRound2(systemSizeKw * SO_ROOF_M2_PER_KW);
  const roofMaxKw = roofAreaM2 === null ? null : Math.floor(roofAreaM2 / SO_ROOF_M2_PER_KW * 4 + 1e-9) / 4;
  const roofFits = roofAreaM2 === null ? null : roofAreaM2 >= roofAreaRequiredM2;
  return {
    monthlyUnits: soRound2(monthlyUnits),
    systemSizeKw,
    tariff: soRound2(tariff),
    surplusRate: soRound2(surplusRate),
    roofAreaM2,
    stateCategory,
    costPerKw: soRound2(costPerKw),
    netMeterCost: soRound2(netMeterCost),
    suggestedSizeKw: soSuggestedSize(monthlyUnits),
    annualUnits,
    annualGenerationUnits,
    monthlyGenerationUnits,
    systemCost,
    subsidy,
    netCost,
    replacedUnits: soRound2(replacedUnits),
    surplusUnits,
    annualSavings,
    monthlySavings,
    paybackYears,
    savings25y,
    co2PerYearT,
    co2_25yT,
    roofAreaRequiredM2,
    roofMaxKw,
    roofFits,
  };
}

