// Home loan prepayment calculator (India).
// The interest saved and the tenure cut by part-prepaying a home
// loan — monthly, as a lump sum, or both — worked out in the browser.
// - Rules (verified 14 November 2026 — see sources.md): EMI =
//   P x r x (1+r)^n / ((1+r)^n - 1), r = annual rate / 12 / 100,
//   n = remaining months. The EMI is used UNROUNDED in the
//   simulation (CredoCalc's own totals prove this: with the rounded
//   EMI the sample gives interest Rs 31,33,031 and prepayments
//   Rs 7,47,484; with the unrounded EMI it gives Rs 31,33,032 and
//   Rs 7,47,485 — exactly what CredoCalc publishes). Only the
//   displayed EMI is rounded to paise.
// - Monthly reducing balance: each month, interest = balance x r;
//   the EMI pays interest first, the rest reduces principal; the
//   monthly part-prepayment then reduces the balance further.
// - CONVENTION (stated on the page): a lump sum is applied at the
//   START of the stated month, before that month's interest accrues;
//   the monthly part-prepayment is added to every EMI from month 1.
//   The loan closes in the month the balance reaches zero; the final
//   payment is adjusted down (interest + remaining balance), and the
//   final month's part-prepayment is only the part still needed after
//   the EMI — never more than the balance, never negative.
// - The five anchors use three lump-sum conventions between them
//   (see math-tests.md): CredoCalc applies a lump "paid in year Y"
//   at the start of month 12(Y-1)+2 (after the first EMI of that
//   year); FinCalculator / MoneyCalculator apply a lump "paid in
//   month M" at the start of month M+1 (after that month's EMI);
//   OptimizeApp applies a lump "paid in year Y" at the start of
//   month 12Y+1 (at the end of that year); CalcNSave applies its
//   lump at the start of month 1 — the same convention as this tool.
// - Reduce tenure (default): keep the EMI, the loan finishes early.
//   Reduce EMI: after each prepayment the EMI is recomputed on the
//   balance then outstanding over the months still left, so the loan
//   still ends near the original date with a smaller EMI. A lump sum
//   applied before a month's EMI is followed by a recompute over the
//   months left including that month; a monthly part-prepayment is
//   followed by a recompute over the months left after that month.
//   This reproduces FinCalculator's reduce-EMI figures exactly (new
//   EMI Rs 38,964, saved Rs 5.09L on their month-13 input).
// - Prepayment charge: chargePct % of the prepayments actually made
//   (a fixed-rate-loan charge; floating-rate loans to individuals
//   carry none under the RBI (Pre-payment Charges on Loans)
//   Directions, 2025 — see sources.md). Interest saved after charge
//   = interest saved - charge.
// - Payoff dates count from November 2026 (the page's as-of month):
//   original payoff = Nov 2026 + remaining months; new payoff =
//   Nov 2026 + new months.
// - Anchors, checked 14 November 2026 against the independent
//   Python model: CredoCalc — Rs 50L @8.5%, 15y, Rs 5,000/mo:
//   EMI Rs 49,236.98, interest saved Rs 7,29,624, 2y 6m sooner
//   (May 2039 vs Nov 2041), 30 fewer EMIs, new interest
//   Rs 31,33,032 vs Rs 38,62,656, outgo Rs 54,236.98, prepayments
//   Rs 7,47,485, Rs 0.98 per Re 1; Rs 10,000/mo saves Rs 12,17,058
//   and finishes 4y 2m early; the full 15-row year table reproduces
//   to the rupee. FinCalculator — Rs 50L @8.5% 20y, Rs 5L lump sum
//   in month 12: interest saved Rs 16.04L, tenure 240 -> 192
//   months, baseline Rs 54.14L, new Rs 38.10L; reduce-EMI mode saves
//   Rs 5.09L with EMI Rs 38,964. CalcNSave — Rs 20L @9% 15y, Rs 2L
//   one-off: about 147 months, about 2.75 years shorter, saves
//   about Rs 4,78,224; live default Rs 25L @8.5% 15y, Rs 5L:
//   EMI Rs 24,618.49, saved Rs 9,43,195, 122 months. MoneyCalculator
//   timing table (Rs 5L at months 6/12/24/36/60/120): Rs 16.80L /
//   Rs 16.04L / Rs 14.57L / Rs 13.20L / Rs 10.69L / Rs 5.71L.
//   OptimizeApp — Rs 50L @9% 30y, Rs 100/day (Rs 3,000/mo): saves
//   Rs 27.92L, 7y 5m off, 89 EMIs gone; the five-row Rs 100/day
//   table and the Ananya example reproduce exactly; the Rs 1L
//   timing table reproduces exactly with their end-of-year
//   convention.
// - Rounding: every amount is computed unrounded; each displayed
//   figure is rounded to paise (half up). Year-table figures are the
//   rounded per-year sums. Interest saved per Re 1 prepaid =
//   interest saved / total prepayments (null when nothing is
//   prepaid).
// - This is an estimate for planning only, not a lender quote.
//   Nothing is sent anywhere: every calculation runs in the browser.
// Conventions (stated on the page):
// - The client sends exactly the 9 HP_KEYS.
// - balance is a finite number from Rs 10,000 up to Rs 10,00,00,000.
//   rate is a finite number from 1 up to 24 (% a year).
//   tenureYears is an integer from 0 up to 30; tenureMonths is an
//   integer from 0 up to 11; the total months are from 1 up to 360.
//   monthlyPrepay is a finite number from Rs 0 up to Rs 10,00,000.
//   lumpSum is a finite number from Rs 0 up to the balance.
//   lumpMonth is an integer from 1 up to the total months.
//   strategy is "tenure" or "emi". chargePct is a finite number
//   from 0 up to 10 (% of the prepayments made).
export const HP_MIN_BALANCE = 10000;
export const HP_MAX_BALANCE = 100000000;
export const HP_MIN_RATE = 1;
export const HP_MAX_RATE = 24;
export const HP_MAX_TENURE_YEARS = 30;
export const HP_MAX_TENURE_MONTHS_PART = 11;
export const HP_MIN_TOTAL_MONTHS = 1;
export const HP_MAX_TOTAL_MONTHS = 360;
export const HP_MAX_MONTHLY_PREPAY = 1000000;
export const HP_MAX_CHARGE_PCT = 10;
export const HP_BASE_YEAR = 2026;
export const HP_BASE_MONTH = 11;
export const HP_MONTH_NAMES = ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr", "May", "Jun", "Jul", "Aug", "Sep", "Oct", "Nov", "Dec"];
export const HP_KEYS = ["balance", "rate", "tenureYears", "tenureMonths", "monthlyPrepay", "lumpSum", "lumpMonth", "strategy", "chargePct"];
export const HP_STRATEGIES = ["tenure", "emi"];
export function hpRound2(x) {
  return Math.floor(x * 100 + 0.5) / 100;
}
export function hpEmi(balance, rate, months) {
  const r = rate / 12 / 100;
  return balance * r * Math.pow(1 + r, months) / (Math.pow(1 + r, months) - 1);
}
export function hpPayoffDate(months) {
  const total = (HP_BASE_YEAR * 12 + (HP_BASE_MONTH - 1)) + months;
  return HP_MONTH_NAMES[total % 12] + " " + (Math.floor(total / 12));
}
export function hpBaselineYears(balance, rate, totalMonths) {
  const r = rate / 12 / 100;
  const emi0 = hpEmi(balance, rate, totalMonths);
  let bal = balance;
  const out = [];
  let acc = 0;
  for (let m = 1; m <= totalMonths; m++) {
    const intr = bal * r;
    acc += intr;
    bal -= (emi0 - intr);
    if (m % 12 === 0 || m === totalMonths) {
      out.push([hpRound2(bal > 0 ? bal : 0), hpRound2(acc)]);
      acc = 0;
    }
  }
  return out;
}
export function hpCompute(input) {
  if (!input || typeof input !== "object") return null;
  const balance = input.balance;
  const rate = input.rate;
  const tenureYears = input.tenureYears;
  const tenureMonths = input.tenureMonths;
  const monthlyPrepay = input.monthlyPrepay;
  const lumpSum = input.lumpSum;
  const lumpMonth = input.lumpMonth;
  const strategy = input.strategy;
  const chargePct = input.chargePct;
  if (typeof balance !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(balance) || balance < HP_MIN_BALANCE || balance > HP_MAX_BALANCE) return null;
  if (typeof rate !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(rate) || rate < HP_MIN_RATE || rate > HP_MAX_RATE) return null;
  if (typeof tenureYears !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(tenureYears) || !Number.isInteger(tenureYears) || tenureYears < 0 || tenureYears > HP_MAX_TENURE_YEARS) return null;
  if (typeof tenureMonths !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(tenureMonths) || !Number.isInteger(tenureMonths) || tenureMonths < 0 || tenureMonths > HP_MAX_TENURE_MONTHS_PART) return null;
  const totalMonths = tenureYears * 12 + tenureMonths;
  if (totalMonths < HP_MIN_TOTAL_MONTHS || totalMonths > HP_MAX_TOTAL_MONTHS) return null;
  if (typeof monthlyPrepay !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(monthlyPrepay) || monthlyPrepay < 0 || monthlyPrepay > HP_MAX_MONTHLY_PREPAY) return null;
  if (typeof lumpSum !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(lumpSum) || lumpSum < 0 || lumpSum > balance) return null;
  if (typeof lumpMonth !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(lumpMonth) || !Number.isInteger(lumpMonth) || lumpMonth < 1 || lumpMonth > totalMonths) return null;
  if (HP_STRATEGIES.indexOf(strategy) === -1) return null;
  if (typeof chargePct !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(chargePct) || chargePct < 0 || chargePct > HP_MAX_CHARGE_PCT) return null;
  const r = rate / 12 / 100;
  const emi0 = hpEmi(balance, rate, totalMonths);
  const baseInterest = emi0 * totalMonths - balance;
  const baseYears = hpBaselineYears(balance, rate, totalMonths);
  let bal = balance;
  let totInt = 0;
  let totPre = 0;
  let months = 0;
  let emi = emi0;
  let emiAfterFirst = null;
  const newYears = [];
  let acc = 0;
  let closed = false;
  for (let m = 1; m <= totalMonths; m++) {
    let prepayThisMonth = 0;
    if (lumpSum && m === lumpMonth) {
      const take = Math.min(lumpSum, bal);
      bal -= take;
      totPre += take;
      prepayThisMonth += take;
      if (bal <= 0.005) {
        bal = 0;
        months = m;
        newYears.push([0, acc]);
        closed = true;
        break;
      }
      if (strategy === "emi") {
        emi = hpEmi(bal, rate, totalMonths - m + 1);
        if (emiAfterFirst === null) emiAfterFirst = emi;
      }
    }
    const intr = bal * r;
    const due = bal + intr;
    const pay = emi + monthlyPrepay;
    if (pay >= due) {
      totInt += intr;
      acc += intr;
      if (monthlyPrepay && due > emi) {
        const prepayFinal = Math.min(monthlyPrepay, due - emi);
        totPre += prepayFinal;
        prepayThisMonth += prepayFinal;
      }
      bal = 0;
      months = m;
      newYears.push([0, acc]);
      closed = true;
      break;
    }
    bal -= (emi - intr);
    const pp = Math.min(monthlyPrepay, bal);
    bal -= pp;
    totPre += pp;
    prepayThisMonth += pp;
    totInt += intr;
    acc += intr;
    months = m;
    if (strategy === "emi" && prepayThisMonth > 0 && m < totalMonths && bal > 0.005) {
      emi = hpEmi(bal, rate, totalMonths - m);
      if (emiAfterFirst === null) emiAfterFirst = emi;
    }
    if (bal <= 0.005) {
      bal = 0;
      newYears.push([0, acc]);
      closed = true;
      break;
    }
    if (m % 12 === 0) {
      newYears.push([bal, acc]);
      acc = 0;
    }
  }
  if (!closed) {
    if (totalMonths % 12 !== 0) {
      newYears.push([bal, acc]);
    }
  }
  const totalYears = Math.floor((totalMonths - 1) / 12) + 1;
  while (newYears.length < totalYears) {
    newYears.push([0, 0]);
  }
  const yearRows = [];
  let cumBase = 0;
  let cumNew = 0;
  for (let y = 0; y < totalYears; y++) {
    const baseRow = baseYears[y];
    const newRow = newYears[y];
    cumBase += baseRow[1];
    cumNew += hpRound2(newRow[1]);
    yearRows.push({
      year: y + 1,
      baseBalance: baseRow[0],
      newBalance: hpRound2(newRow[0]),
      baseInterest: baseRow[1],
      newInterest: hpRound2(newRow[1]),
      savedSoFar: hpRound2(cumBase - cumNew)
    });
  }
  const newEmi = strategy === "tenure" ? emi0 : (emiAfterFirst === null ? emi0 : emiAfterFirst);
  const emiR = hpRound2(emi0);
  const newEmiR = hpRound2(newEmi);
  const baseInterestR = hpRound2(baseInterest);
  const newInterestR = hpRound2(totInt);
  const totalPreR = hpRound2(totPre);
  const interestSaved = hpRound2(baseInterestR - newInterestR);
  const charge = hpRound2(chargePct / 100 * totalPreR);
  const tenureSaved = totalMonths - months;
  return {
    balance: hpRound2(balance),
    rate: hpRound2(rate),
    tenureYears,
    tenureMonths,
    totalMonths,
    monthlyPrepay: hpRound2(monthlyPrepay),
    lumpSum: hpRound2(lumpSum),
    lumpMonth,
    strategy,
    chargePct: hpRound2(chargePct),
    emi: emiR,
    baselineMonths: totalMonths,
    baselineTotalInterest: baseInterestR,
    baselineTotalPaid: hpRound2(baseInterestR + balance),
    newMonths: months,
    newEmi: newEmiR,
    newTotalInterest: newInterestR,
    newEmiPayments: hpRound2(newInterestR + balance),
    totalPrepayments: totalPreR,
    totalCashOut: hpRound2(newInterestR + balance + totalPreR),
    interestSaved,
    interestSavedPct: baseInterestR > 0 ? hpRound2(interestSaved / baseInterestR * 100) : 0,
    chargeAmount: charge,
    interestSavedAfterCharge: hpRound2(interestSaved - charge),
    tenureSavedMonths: tenureSaved,
    tenureSavedYears: Math.floor(tenureSaved / 12),
    tenureSavedMonthsRemainder: tenureSaved % 12,
    emisSaved: tenureSaved,
    payoffDate: hpPayoffDate(months),
    payoffDateBaseline: hpPayoffDate(totalMonths),
    monthlyOutgo: hpRound2(newEmiR + monthlyPrepay),
    savedPerRupee: totalPreR > 0 ? hpRound2(interestSaved / totalPreR) : null,
    yearRows
  };
}

