// Dearness Allowance (DA) calculator (India), 7th Central Pay Commission.
// The monthly DA (or Dearness Relief, DR, for pensioners) on basic pay
// or basic pension, the yearly DA, the pay with DA, and the arrears for a
// retrospective rate rise — worked out in the browser.
// - Rules (verified 14 November 2026 — see sources.md): DA is a
//   percentage of basic pay in the 7th CPC Pay Matrix level, revised
//   twice a year (1 January and 1 July) from AICPI-IW averages. The
//   current rate is 63% from 1 July 2026: approved by the Union Cabinet
//   on 28 October 2026 (PIB Release ID 2329484) and notified by the
//   Department of Expenditure OM No. 1/2(i)/2026-E.II(B) dated
//   29 October 2026, up from 60% from 1 January 2026 (DoE OM No.
//   1/1(i)/2026-E.II(B) dated 22 April 2026; Cabinet approval
//   18 April 2026). Pensioners get Dearness Relief at the same rate on
//   basic pension (DoPPW OM No. 42/02/2024-P&PW(D)/E-9475 dated
//   4 November 2026).
// - Rounding (DoE OM, 22 April 2026): for employees, a fraction of
//   50 paise or more rounds up to the next rupee and a smaller fraction
//   is ignored — DA is rounded to the nearest rupee, half up. For
//   pensioners, DR with any fraction of a rupee is rounded up to the
//   next rupee. The two rules differ: on a basic pension of Rs 44,905
//   at 63% the raw DR is Rs 28,290.15, so DR is Rs 28,291 while the
//   same figures as DA give Rs 28,290.
// - Arrears: month by month, DA at the new rate minus DA at the old
//   rate (each rounded first), times the number of months paid at the
//   old rate. No arrears were paid for the COVID freeze (January 2020
//   to June 2021): the instalments were withheld and released together
//   from 1 July 2021, so a rise announced late is the only source of
//   arrears. Arrears are taxed in the year they are received; relief
//   can be claimed under Section 157(1) of the Income-tax Act, 2025
//   in Form 39 (Section 89(1) / Form 10E under the old law).
// - NPS: NPS contributions are 10% (employee) and 14% (Government) of
//   basic pay plus DA, so 10% is usually recovered from DA arrears for
//   NPS members; old-pension-scheme employees have no NPS deduction.
//   The calculator deducts 10% of positive arrears only, for employees
//   who tick the NPS box; pensioners never get an NPS deduction.
// - DA is paid on basic pay ONLY: not on HRA, and on transport
//   allowance only in two narrow cases (Levels 1-2 drawing the lower
//   Rs 1,350 / Rs 900 band, and the Level 14+ car-option rate) — every
//   other TA band is flat. TA is therefore NOT modelled; the page says
//   so. State government employees follow their own orders and rates;
//   the calculator accepts any rate, so a state rate can be entered.
// - The 8th Pay Commission is not in force yet (no date officially
//   fixed as of 14 November 2026); the calculator works for any rate,
//   so it stays usable when the 8th CPC lands and DA restarts near 0%.
// - Anchors, checked 14 November 2026 against the independent Python
//   model: TabSalary — basic Rs 56,100 at 60% (January 2026) gives DA
//   Rs 33,660 a month; the same basic at 46% (July 2023) gives
//   Rs 25,806. hrcalcy — Rs 56,100, 60% to 63%: DA Rs 33,660 to
//   Rs 35,343, arrears Rs 1,683 a month, Rs 6,732 for 4 months
//   (July to October 2026), NPS 10% Rs 673, net Rs 6,059; on a basic
//   pension of Rs 30,000, DR Rs 18,000 to Rs 18,900, arrears Rs 900 a
//   month, Rs 3,600 for 4 months. indianpaycalculator (Ravi) — basic
//   Rs 44,900, 46% to 50% from 1 January 2024, 2 months: old DA
//   Rs 20,654, new DA Rs 22,450, arrears Rs 1,796 a month, total
//   Rs 3,592. hrcalcy 7th CPC salary — basic Rs 44,900 at 60% gives
//   DA Rs 26,940.
// - Rounding example (TabSalary): Rs 2,145.49 pays as Rs 2,145 and
//   Rs 2,145.50 pays as Rs 2,146 — reproduced here as basic Rs 42,910
//   at 5% (Rs 2,145.50 -> Rs 2,146) and Rs 42,909 at 5% (Rs 2,145.45
//   -> Rs 2,145).
// - This is an estimate for planning only, not pay advice. Nothing is
//   sent anywhere: every calculation runs in the browser.
// Conventions (stated on the page):
// - The client sends exactly the 6 DA_KEYS.
// - personType is "employee" (DA) or "pensioner" (DR). basicPay is the
//   monthly basic pay (employee) or basic pension (pensioner) in
//   rupees, from Rs 1,000 to Rs 2,50,000. daRate and oldRate are
//   percentages from 0 to 100. arrearsMonths is a whole number from 0
//   to 12. nps is "yes" or "no" (NPS 10% deduction on arrears,
//   employees only).
export const DA_MIN_BASIC = 1000;
export const DA_MAX_BASIC = 250000;
export const DA_MAX_RATE = 100;
export const DA_MAX_MONTHS = 12;
export const DA_NPS_RATE = 0.10;
export const DA_KEYS = ["personType", "basicPay", "daRate", "oldRate", "arrearsMonths", "nps"];
export const DA_PERSON_TYPES = ["employee", "pensioner"];
export const DA_NPS_OPTIONS = ["yes", "no"];
export function daRound(x) {
  return Math.floor(x + 0.5);
}
export function daRoundUp(x) {
  return Math.ceil(x - 1e-9);
}
export function daRound2(x) {
  return Math.floor(x * 100 + 0.5) / 100;
}
export function daAmountFor(basicPay, rate, personType) {
  const raw = basicPay * rate / 100;
  return personType === "pensioner" ? daRoundUp(raw) : daRound(raw);
}
export function daCompute(input) {
  if (!input || typeof input !== "object") return null;
  const personType = input.personType;
  const basicPay = input.basicPay;
  const daRate = input.daRate;
  const oldRate = input.oldRate;
  const arrearsMonths = input.arrearsMonths;
  const nps = input.nps;
  if (DA_PERSON_TYPES.indexOf(personType) === -1) return null;
  if (typeof basicPay !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(basicPay) || basicPay < DA_MIN_BASIC || basicPay > DA_MAX_BASIC) return null;
  if (typeof daRate !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(daRate) || daRate < 0 || daRate > DA_MAX_RATE) return null;
  if (typeof oldRate !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(oldRate) || oldRate < 0 || oldRate > DA_MAX_RATE) return null;
  if (typeof arrearsMonths !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(arrearsMonths) || !Number.isInteger(arrearsMonths) || arrearsMonths < 0 || arrearsMonths > DA_MAX_MONTHS) return null;
  if (DA_NPS_OPTIONS.indexOf(nps) === -1) return null;
  const daAmount = daAmountFor(basicPay, daRate, personType);
  const daAnnual = daAmount * 12;
  const daAtOldRate = daAmountFor(basicPay, oldRate, personType);
  const rateRise = daRound2(daRate - oldRate);
  const arrearsPerMonth = daAmount - daAtOldRate;
  const arrearsTotal = arrearsPerMonth * arrearsMonths;
  const npsDeduction = personType === "employee" && nps === "yes" && arrearsTotal > 0 ? daRound(arrearsTotal * DA_NPS_RATE) : 0;
  const arrearsNet = arrearsTotal - npsDeduction;
  const grossWithDa = basicPay + daAmount;
  const daSharePct = daRound2(daAmount / grossWithDa * 100);
  return {
    personType,
    basicPay,
    daRate,
    oldRate,
    arrearsMonths,
    nps,
    daAmount,
    daAnnual,
    daAtOldRate,
    rateRise,
    arrearsPerMonth,
    arrearsTotal,
    npsDeduction,
    arrearsNet,
    grossWithDa,
    daSharePct,
  };
}

