// Sleep Calculator (India).
// Bedtimes and wake-up times that line up with 90-minute sleep
// cycles, so the alarm catches you between cycles, not in the middle
// of deep sleep — worked out in the browser.
// - Rules (verified 14 November 2026 — see sources.md): sleep comes
//   in cycles of about 90 minutes. A bedtime (or wake-up time) is the
//   anchor time minus/plus the time to fall asleep plus a whole
//   number of cycles: bedtime = wake-up time - onset - cycles x
//   cycle length; wake-up = bedtime + onset + cycles x cycle length.
//   Times are minutes from midnight (0-1439), wrapped mod 1440, so a
//   bedtime after midnight — or a wake-up after noon for a day
//   sleeper — wraps to the next day.
// - Modes: "wake" (the anchor is the wake-up time, results are
//   bedtimes), "bed" (the anchor is the bedtime, results are wake-up
//   times), "now" (the anchor is the current time, results are
//   wake-up times). Onset (time to fall asleep) is 0-30 minutes,
//   default 15. Cycle length is 80-100 minutes, default 90.
// - Rows are shown for 6, 5, 4 and 3 cycles. Total sleep = cycles x
//   cycle length. Recommended sleep ranges (National Sleep
//   Foundation): child 6-13 years 9-11 hours, teenager 14-17 years
//   8-10 hours, adult 18-64 years 7-9 hours, older adult 65+ years
//   7-8 hours.
// - Verdicts: total sleep below the range is "short" (3 cycles is
//   "too short"); above the range is "long"; inside the range is
//   "recommended".
// - Recommended cycles: the fewest cycles whose total sleep reaches
//   the bottom of the age group's range; if no cycle count reaches
//   it (a child with an 80-minute cycle: 6 x 80 = 480 < 540), 6
//   cycles. With the defaults (90-minute cycle): adult 5, older
//   adult 5, teenager 6, child 6.
// - Anchors, checked 14 November 2026 against the independent Python
//   model (all fetched the same day): sleepcalculator.in's bedtime
//   chart reproduces exactly for all eight wake-up times (wake 6:00
//   AM -> 8:45 PM / 10:15 PM / 11:45 PM for 6, 5 and 4 cycles; wake
//   7:00 AM -> 9:45 PM / 11:15 PM / 12:45 AM; wake 5:00 AM -> 7:45
//   PM / 9:15 PM / 10:45 PM; wake 8:00 AM -> 10:45 PM / 12:15 AM /
//   1:45 AM). sleepcalculator.in's FAQ reproduces with a 0-minute
//   onset: wake 6:00 AM -> fall asleep 10:30 PM (5 cycles) or 9:00
//   PM (6 cycles). debasisbhattacharjee.com's worked example
//   reproduces: wake 07:00 with 15 minutes to fall asleep -> 21:45
//   (6), 23:15 (5), 00:45 (4), 02:15 (3). instantcalchub.com
//   reproduces: wake 7:00 AM, 15 minutes, 5 cycles -> 11:15 PM, 6
//   cycles -> 9:45 PM. icalcapp.com's bedtime table reproduces with
//   a 14-minute onset: wake 6:00 AM -> 11:46 PM (4), 10:16 PM (5),
//   8:46 PM (6). sleepcalculator.in's routines reproduce: school
//   student wake 6:00 AM -> lights out 10:15 PM (5 cycles); office
//   commuter wake 6:30 AM -> 10:45 PM; night shift, bed 5:45 AM ->
//   wake 1:30 PM (5 cycles); Sehri wake 4:15 AM -> 10:00 PM (4
//   cycles); Brahma Muhurta wake 4:30 AM -> 8:45 PM (5 cycles).
// - Near-matches, stated honestly (see sources.md): aimindia.in's
//   two worked scenarios do NOT reproduce at their stated input
//   times — scenario 1 (wake 7:00 AM, 14-minute onset) quotes 10:16
//   PM / 11:46 PM / 1:16 AM, but the model gives 9:46 PM / 11:16 PM
//   / 12:46 AM; the quoted figures reproduce exactly for a 7:30 AM
//   wake-up. Scenario 2 (bed 11:00 PM) quotes 4:44 / 6:14 / 7:44 /
//   9:14 AM, but the model gives 3:44 / 5:14 / 6:44 / 8:14 AM; the
//   quoted figures reproduce exactly for a midnight bedtime. Both
//   scenarios are one hour off in the stated input time.
//   icalcapp.com's FAQ answer (wake 6:00 AM, 14-minute onset) quotes
//   10:46 PM (5 cycles) and 9:16 PM (6 cycles); the model gives
//   10:16 PM and 8:46 PM — the FAQ figures imply 7 and 8.5 hours of
//   sleep, not 7.5 and 9, and contradict the same page's bedtime
//   table, which reproduces exactly. icalcapp.com's worked example
//   for wake 6:30 AM quotes 12:15 AM (5 cycles) and 10:45 PM (6
//   cycles); the model gives 10:45 PM (5) and 9:15 PM (6) — and the
//   page's own backward chain (4:45, 3:15, 1:45, 12:15 AM, 10:45 PM)
//   confirms 12:15 AM is the 4th step back, not the 5th.
// - aimindia.in and icalcapp.com default to a 14-minute onset; this
//   calculator defaults to 15 minutes (sleepcalculator.in,
//   debasisbhattacharjee.com and instantcalchub.com all use 15) and
//   lets the user change it from 0 to 30.
// - India, by the numbers (fetched 14 November 2026): a 2025
//   systematic review in the Indian Journal of Medical Research
//   found 25.7% of Indians suffer from insomnia (aimindia.in); the
//   Great Indian Sleep Scorecard 2025 found 55% of Indians sleep
//   past midnight and 40% get less than six hours a night
//   (aimindia.in). Fitbit 2024 averages (icalcapp.com): India
//   overall 7h 01m (bed 11:45 PM, wake 6:46 AM); Bengaluru 6h 53m
//   (12:02 AM - 6:55 AM); Mumbai 6h 55m (11:58 PM - 6:53 AM); Delhi
//   6h 48m (11:50 PM - 6:38 AM); Kolkata 7h 08m (11:32 PM - 6:40
//   AM). All five city rows are arithmetically consistent
//   (wake - bedtime = the stated average).
// - This is an estimate for planning only, not medical advice.
//   Cycles average about 90 minutes and vary from person to person
//   and through the night (about 70 to 120 minutes). See a doctor
//   for persistent sleep problems. Nothing is sent anywhere: every
//   calculation runs in the browser.
// Conventions (stated on the page):
// - The client sends exactly the 5 SL_KEYS.
// - mode is "wake", "bed" or "now". timeMinutes is minutes from
//   midnight, a whole number from 0 to 1439. onset is the time to
//   fall asleep, a whole number from 0 to 30 minutes (default 15).
//   cycleLength is the length of one sleep cycle, a whole number
//   from 80 to 100 minutes (default 90). ageGroup is "child",
//   "teen", "adult" or "older" (default "adult").
export const SL_MIN_ONSET = 0;
export const SL_MAX_ONSET = 30;
export const SL_MIN_CYCLE = 80;
export const SL_MAX_CYCLE = 100;
export const SL_DEFAULT_ONSET = 15;
export const SL_DEFAULT_CYCLE = 90;
export const SL_AGE_GROUPS = ["child", "teen", "adult", "older"];
export const SL_AGE_RANGES = { child: [540, 660], teen: [480, 600], adult: [420, 540], older: [420, 480] };
export const SL_KEYS = ["mode", "timeMinutes", "onset", "cycleLength", "ageGroup"];
export function slMod1440(m) {
  return ((m % 1440) + 1440) % 1440;
}
export function slFormatTime(minutes) {
  const m = slMod1440(minutes);
  const h = Math.floor(m / 60);
  const mm = m % 60;
  const ap = h < 12 ? "AM" : "PM";
  const h12 = h % 12 === 0 ? 12 : h % 12;
  return h12 + ":" + String(mm).padStart(2, "0") + " " + ap;
}
export function slHoursLabel(totalMinutes) {
  const h = totalMinutes / 60;
  if (h === Math.floor(h)) return h + " hours";
  return h.toFixed(1) + " hours";
}
export function slRecommendedCycles(cycleLength, ageGroup) {
  const lo = SL_AGE_RANGES[ageGroup][0];
  for (let n = 3; n <= 6; n++) {
    if (n * cycleLength >= lo) return n;
  }
  return 6;
}
export function slCompute(input) {
  if (!input || typeof input !== "object") return null;
  const mode = input.mode;
  const timeMinutes = input.timeMinutes;
  const onset = input.onset;
  const cycleLength = input.cycleLength;
  const ageGroup = input.ageGroup;
  if (mode !== "wake" && mode !== "bed" && mode !== "now") return null;
  if (typeof timeMinutes !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(timeMinutes) || !Number.isInteger(timeMinutes) || timeMinutes < 0 || timeMinutes > 1439) return null;
  if (typeof onset !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(onset) || !Number.isInteger(onset) || onset < SL_MIN_ONSET || onset > SL_MAX_ONSET) return null;
  if (typeof cycleLength !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(cycleLength) || !Number.isInteger(cycleLength) || cycleLength < SL_MIN_CYCLE || cycleLength > SL_MAX_CYCLE) return null;
  if (typeof ageGroup !== "string" || SL_AGE_GROUPS.indexOf(ageGroup) === -1) return null;
  const range = SL_AGE_RANGES[ageGroup];
  const lo = range[0];
  const hi = range[1];
  const rec = slRecommendedCycles(cycleLength, ageGroup);
  const rows = [];
  for (let n = 6; n >= 3; n--) {
    const total = n * cycleLength;
    const minutes = mode === "wake" ? slMod1440(timeMinutes - onset - total) : slMod1440(timeMinutes + onset + total);
    let verdict;
    if (total < lo) verdict = n === 3 ? "too short" : "short";
    else if (total > hi) verdict = "long";
    else verdict = "recommended";
    rows.push({
      cycles: n,
      totalSleepMinutes: total,
      totalSleepLabel: slHoursLabel(total),
      minutes,
      label: slFormatTime(minutes),
      verdict,
      recommended: n === rec,
    });
  }
  const recRow = rows.find((r) => r.cycles === rec);
  const ageLabels = { child: "Child (6-13 years)", teen: "Teenager (14-17 years)", adult: "Adult (18-64 years)", older: "Older adult (65+ years)" };
  return {
    mode,
    timeMinutes,
    timeLabel: slFormatTime(timeMinutes),
    onset,
    cycleLength,
    ageGroup,
    ageGroupLabel: ageLabels[ageGroup],
    rangeMinMinutes: lo,
    rangeMaxMinutes: hi,
    rangeLabel: Math.floor(lo / 60) + "-" + Math.floor(hi / 60) + " hours",
    recommendedCycles: rec,
    recommendedMinutes: recRow.minutes,
    recommendedLabel: recRow.label,
    recommendedTotalSleepMinutes: recRow.totalSleepMinutes,
    recommendedTotalSleepLabel: recRow.totalSleepLabel,
    resultKind: mode === "wake" ? "bedtime" : "wake-up time",
    rows,
  };
}

