          <p>
            Turnover = buy value + sell value (for options, the premium values). Brokerage is charged per executed order: Zerodha ₹0 on delivery, the lower of ₹20 or 0.03% on intraday and futures, ₹20 flat on options; Groww and Angel One the lower of ₹20 or 0.1% (minimum ₹5) on equity and ₹20 flat on F&O; Upstox ₹20 flat on delivery, the lower of ₹20 or 0.1% on intraday, the lower of ₹20 or 0.05% on futures and ₹20 on options; flat ₹20 is ₹20 per order everywhere. STT: delivery 0.1% on buy and sell, intraday 0.025% on sell, futures 0.05% on sell, options 0.15% of the premium sold (Finance Act 2026, from 1 April 2026). Exchange transaction charges: NSE equity 0.00307%, futures 0.00183%, options 0.03553% of premium (from 1 March 2026, IPFT included); BSE equity 0.00375%, futures 0, options 0.0325% of premium. SEBI fee ₹10 per crore of turnover. Stamp duty on the buy side: delivery 0.015%, intraday 0.003%, futures 0.002%, options 0.003%. DP charge on delivery sells only: Zerodha ₹15.34 per scrip including GST, other brokers ₹20 + GST (₹23.60). GST 18% on brokerage + exchange charges + SEBI fee. Break-even is the sell price at which net profit is exactly zero, solved by bisection. Money is rounded to paise; each line is rounded, and the total is the unrounded sum rounded to paise.
          </p>
          <p>
