                <p class="calc-small" id="le-steps-note">Encashment = (Basic + DA) ÷ divisor × leave days. The exemption is the least of the four limbs: the amount received, 10 months' average salary, the ₹25,00,000 ceiling less prior claims, and the cash equivalent of leave capped at 30 days per completed year, valued at (salary ÷ 30).</p>
