// Road Tax Calculator.
// How much road tax a new private car or two-wheeler costs in 16 Indian
// states, worked out in the browser.
// - Inputs: state (16 states), vehicle type (private car / two-wheeler),
//   fuel (petrol / diesel / CNG / electric), ex-showroom price in rupees,
//   optional insurance amount entered by the visitor (default 0 — this
//   tool never estimates insurance).
// - road tax = ex-showroom price x rate / 100, rounded half-up to whole
//   rupees. The rate comes from the state's price-band table for the
//   vehicle type and fuel. Bands are "not exceeding <limit>" (price <=
//   limit) UNLESS marked below=true ("below <limit>", price < limit):
//   Telangana cars and Bihar cars/bikes use below=true at the 5/10/20 lakh
//   and 8/15 lakh steps, because their sources' own price-point tables
//   show the higher band applying at exactly that price (mycarhelpline:
//   Telangana Rs.5,00,000 -> 14%, Rs.10,00,000 -> 17%; Bihar Rs.8,00,000
//   -> 10%, Rs.15,00,000 -> 12%).
// - registration fee = Rs.600 (car / LMV) or Rs.300 (motorcycle), CMVR
//   Rule 81; Rs.0 for electric vehicles (central RC fee exempt).
// - on-road total = ex-showroom + road tax + registration fee + insurance.
// - West Bengal two-wheelers pay a FIXED amount by engine size (Rs.1,560
//   up to 80cc, Rs.3,125 for 80-170cc, Rs.4,685 for 170-250cc, Rs.6,250
//   above 250cc); this tool uses Rs.3,125 (the common 80-170cc band) and
//   says so on the page. Maharashtra bikes use 11% (the 100-299cc band;
//   10% up to 99cc, 12% above 300cc) and Rajasthan bikes use 8% (up to
//   200cc; 13% for 200-500cc, 15% above 500cc); both are stated on the page.
// - EV treatment is per state: most states exempt EVs; Karnataka charges
//   10% above Rs.25 lakh, Kerala 5% up to Rs.15 lakh then 8%, Haryana 5%
//   above Rs.20 lakh, Gujarat 1%, West Bengal 2%, Madhya Pradesh 4%,
//   Odisha 5% (cars; bikes 5% in Kerala, 1% in Gujarat, 4% in Madhya
//   Pradesh, 5% in Odisha, exempt elsewhere).
// - DOCUMENTED DIFFERENCES (not errors): competitors disagree with this
//   tool on four figures, and the page states each one. GoDigit's worked
//   example charges a Rs.1 lakh Telangana bike 9% (Rs.9,000); the banded
//   schedule charges 12% for Rs.50,000-1 lakh, so this tool gives
//   Rs.12,000. feescalculator's worked example charges a Rs.1 lakh Delhi
//   motorcycle 6% (Rs.6,000); the Delhi schedule charges 8% above
//   Rs.60,000, so this tool gives Rs.8,000. InvestVerdict's worked example
//   charges a Rs.10 lakh Karnataka car 17% (Rs.1,70,000); this tool applies
//   14% because the band reads "not exceeding Rs.10 lakh" (transclew's
//   Rs.10 lakh table agrees: 14%, Rs.1,40,000). transclew charges a
//   Rs.10 lakh Telangana car 18% (Rs.1,80,000); mycarhelpline, bankbazaar
//   and gomechanic charge 17% (Rs.1,70,000) for the Rs.10-20 lakh band, so
//   this tool gives Rs.1,70,000. GoDigit's own Telangana car table
//   (3%/6%/8%/9%) contradicts its own 12% worked example and the
//   13/14/17/18% schedule three other sources state; this tool uses
//   13/14/17/18%.
// - The sample: Delhi petrol car, Rs.10,00,000 ex-showroom, no insurance
//   -> 7% road tax, Rs.70,000; registration Rs.600; on-road Rs.10,70,600.
// - Rounding is round-half-up with a 1e-9 nudge: road tax to whole rupees;
//   totals are whole rupees (price + rounded tax + fee + insurance).
//   Derived quantities are computed from the unrounded intermediates.
// - Validation: state must be one of the 16 listed states; vehicleType
//   "car" or "bike"; fuel "petrol"/"diesel"/"cng"/"electric"; price
//   10,000-50,000,000; insurance 0-10,000,000 (0 means not entered).
//   Invalid inputs return null, never a result.
// - SELF-CONTAINMENT NOTE (16 Nov 2026): roadtaxIsNum, roadtaxIsInt,
//   roadtaxR2, roadtaxR0 and every roadtaxFmt* helper are EXPORTED (not
//   plain module-level helpers) so that apply.py copies them into the
//   embedded browser client along with the other pure functions. The
//   363-367 chain leaves the equivalent helpers behind, so those
//   calculators throw a ReferenceError in the browser when Convert is
//   pressed; this pack must not repeat that. Every helper in this file
//   is exported.
