        <p>Honest limits: the calculator charges interest once a month on the balance — interest = balance × APR ÷ 12 ÷ 100. Real cards usually charge interest daily, which costs very slightly more. It does not add 18% GST on the interest, late-payment fees, annual fees or other charges, so the real cost is higher — Zarth's figures include 18% GST on the interest, which is why they are bigger than this page's interest-only figures. The minimum due is 5% of the balance plus that month's interest, or the ₹200 floor, whichever is higher, following HDFC Bank's published rule; other issuers differ — Zarth reports that SBI and Axis charge the interest in full plus 2% of the balance. CreditBharosa's minimum-only totals do not reproduce here because they apply the 5% to the opening balance only; CredoCalc and Rupeka reproduce exactly.</p>
