        <p>Honest limits: the total cost of ownership here is simple — price plus energy plus maintenance minus resale, with NO inflation and NO financing cost. finin2min.com's published totals over 8 years include fuel and electricity inflation and financing assumptions, so this page does not reproduce them; the shape — a higher purchase price recovered through lower running costs — is the same. Insurance is NOT included: add it to the maintenance fields if you want it counted. Resale defaults come from depreciation of about 16% a year for the EV and about 12% a year for petrol or diesel (evvsgascarcost.com), and both resale fields are editable. CO2 uses the grid factor 0.72 kg/kWh and petrol 2.31 kg/L (techovn.com), and diesel 2.68 kg/L (finin2min.com) — the diesel factor is citable, so diesel CO2 rows are shown, not left blank. Documented differences, all from competitors multiplying their own rounded per-km figures: devcalc.in shows ₹6.66/km for ₹100 a litre at 15 km/L while the exact division is ₹6.67; evvsgascarcost.com's 80% home, 20% public annual saving is ₹63,840 from its rounded ₹5.32/km while the exact model figure is ₹63,867; evcommunity.in's ₹1,02,060 a year comes from its rounded ₹5.67/km while the exact figure is ₹1,02,000; its Nexon figures (₹1,950 and ₹8,550 a month) come from its rounded ₹1.30/km while the exact figures are ₹1,951 and ₹8,549; and techovn's 262 kg of CO2 a year comes from the unrounded 14 kWh per 100 km while at the 7.14 km/kWh entered here the exact figure is 261 kg — this page shows the exact figure in every case. Monthly figures are the annual figures ÷ 12, and the yearly figures come from the unrounded cost per km, never from the rounded monthly figure. Rounding is round-half-up.</p>
