    <section class="calc-section" id="methodology">
      <div class="calc-wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Methodology and honest limits</h2>
        </div>
        <p>${e(p.methodology)}</p>
        <p>${e(p.modelNote)}</p>
        <p>Honest limits: the model assumes the basic pay you type is the one on your pay slip and the city class is the one your posting carries. It does not model the Level 1–2 transport allowance exception for basic pay of ₹24,200 or more, or the Level 14+ official-car transport allowance option. CGEGIS is not deducted, because the pay-level to group mapping is not officially verified. Income tax is an estimate under the new regime for FY 2026-27; the exact figure depends on other income and deductions. This is not financial advice.</p>
        <p>Documented differences: (1) Palz's net is ₹60 lower because it deducts CGEGIS, which this page does not deduct because the pay-level to group mapping is not officially verified. (2) HR Calcy's net is ₹200 lower because it deducts Karnataka professional tax; this page leaves professional tax at ₹0 unless you enter it. (3) FinCalculator's ₹1,09,134 is gross minus NPS only, not the in-hand pay — this page's net is ₹1,01,433.83. (4) MyJar's HRA tier at 53% DA is stale — 30%/20%/10% applies once DA crosses 50%. (5) Competitor figures are rounded as printed; differences under ₹2 on a component and under 0.1% on a total are rounding. DA 63% is current as of 16 November 2026 and is an editable input. Rounding here is round-half-up.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

