    <section class="calc-section soft" id="official">
      <div class="calc-wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>What is official and what is not</h2>
        </div>
        <p><strong>Official.</strong> The Union Cabinet approved the Terms of Reference on 28 October 2025, and the Department of Expenditure constituted the 8th Central Pay Commission by resolution dated 3 November 2025. The Chair is Justice Ranjana Prakash Desai, with Prof. Pulak Ghosh as part-time member. The Commission has 18 months to report — around May 2027 — and its recommendations are normally expected to take effect from 1 January 2026. DA is 63% from 1 July 2026.</p>
        <p><strong>Not official.</strong> No fitment factor and no pay matrix has been notified. The fitment factors on this page — 1.92, 2.57, 2.86 and 3.83 — are media-reported scenarios: 1.92 is the widely reported consensus projection, 2.57 is the 7th Pay Commission's factor, 2.86 is the reported upper end of a 2.28–2.86 range, and 3.83 is a staff-side demand from the NC-JCM memorandum, not a decision. The HRA rates after the revision have not been notified either — this page applies the current 30%/20%/10% tiers as a stated assumption. DA is expected to restart at 0% once the new basic absorbs the current 63% — a factor of 1.63 does exactly that — but that too is the usual pattern, not a notified rule; the tool lets you change the DA rate.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

