        <p>The EMI scales with the loan amount, because the formula is linear in the principal: ${moneyText(5000000)} costs ${money2Text(bleCompute({ loanAmount: 5000000, interestRate: 14, tenureMonths: 60, loanType: "term", processingFeePct: 1 }).emi)} a month at 14% over 60 months — five times the ${money2Text(bleCompute({ loanAmount: 1000000, interestRate: 14, tenureMonths: 60, loanType: "term", processingFeePct: 1 }).emi)} on ${moneyText(1000000)}. Every figure in the table is at 14% a year, 60 months, term loan, 1% fee — change any of those and the EMI moves.</p>
